  ('zcrm_1579374000131579024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011919234', 'Casey Hebb', NULL, '1-11-24 Casey is unexpectedly pregnant. Casey thought she didn''t have maternity benefits with Sedera and was almost going to cancel. They''ve been very happy with Sedera so far. I educated her on the maternity benefits which she is thrilled about. She also thought there was some cap on sharing of $250K which is not the case. I sent the maternity sharing guidelines section from the Select+ current guidelines. She''s thrilled to keep Sedera for their family. I let her know to open the Need right away and they will coach her in the process. She also wants to use the Boulder Birthing Center with midwifes and such. She has no intention of doing a planned C-Section which has a higher IUA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-11 13:16:14', '2024-01-11 13:16:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131579019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063253037', 'Bobbi Georgeton', NULL, '1-11-24 Bobbi called bc her accountant is telling her she needs to set up a 125 Cafeteria Plan in order to simply pay for the HSA out of her business. She''s deciding not to bother since many folks pay from the business account and deduct it as an expense. She''s getting a new accountant this year anyhow, since he''s retiring. She also has her neck surgery scheduled for Jan. 22nd as long as she is better from having RV right now. She wants to fund the HSA fully and use that money to pay her ded for the surgery. I suggested leaving a min balance in the account in case she wants to keep the account alive in the future. She''s all set for now and super appreciative.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-11 12:54:33', '2024-01-11 12:54:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131562050', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000074947065', 'Andrew Evans', NULL, '01.11.2024 Andrew called regarding his annual physical - 8/1/2023 - with a lipid panel and more not being covered.
I empowered him with the knowledge of his plan in detail to better understand how to speak to it and guide the providers on their part.
Separate preventive coding from diagnostic.
Bill planstin via phone number on card.
He understood. Then I gave him two steps of actions:
1-Call provider to direct them to call Planstin NOW to bill them
2-Have a 3-way with PLanstin and Me NOW - to settle and make sure UCHealth did not try to bill, and if not what are his options from here.

Nikita from Planstin shared that UCHealth did not bill PLanstin, and to avoid having to talk to UCHealth, connect the CLAIMS dept at Planstin with the UCHealth billing dept to settle the matter. Andrew will email: claims@planstin.com  NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-01-11 12:47:28', '2024-01-11 13:23:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131562045', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000038529382', 'Mitchell Magdovitz', NULL, '01.11.20.24 Mitchell called to get guidance on how to submit his bills, to Sedera. I sent him the email with all the instruction.', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-01-11 12:41:48', '2024-01-11 12:41:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131568008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000074947065', 'Andrew Evans', NULL, '1/11/24: Devon called in to inquire about how to submit a sharing request to zion health, showed her how she can do so. -WU', 'Willis Upton', 'Willis Upton', '2024-01-11 12:38:03', '2024-01-11 12:38:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131579014', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000047153471', 'Thomas Ferguson', NULL, '1-11-24 Thomas called bc he''s having a terrible experience with Sedera. He received an email from his Needs Advocate Mikey Nunez stating Aspen Valley Hospital isn''t cash friendly for his ER visit! He can''t choose the perfect hospital when needing to go to the ER! Sounds like Mikey retracted but it''s causing Thomas great anxiety in making sure his Need will be properly shared. If not, he will get trad ins. by the 15th and get further legal assistance to fight this issue. He previously had a separate Need with Sedera, went through their 2nd Opinion program and didn''t get what he needed. He was paired with a bad dr. and pathetic wheelchair that he says would have broken within days of use. He couldn''t use their recommendations, so all of his time and efforts were not worth his time. He still has an open wound from that issue as it''s unresolved. He''s forwarding his email from Mikey to me to help him.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-11 12:36:09', '2024-01-11 12:36:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131579003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000141390002', 'Michael Earle', NULL, '1-11-24 Christina and Michael are now looking at Select Health Value Gold $1500 Medical Deductible for $1061.97 to give Christina affordable  Specialist visits, low ded and Michael affordable meds. He needs 1 of the following for asthma (? or something similar). Symbicort $247 cash) is what''s working for him but it''s expensive. So, they are going to try Fluticosone/Salmeterol $100 cash or program for $30), or Wixela Inhub  $86 cash or Breo $161 cash all on GoodRX. Instead with the Select Health Value Gold $1500 Medical Deductible, he''ll have a $250 ded and then 25% or 50% coinsurance.  With them both on the plan they are getting a $749.43 APTC with income around $130K. Once Christina moves off the plan in 4 months for Medicare, the APTC will decrease substantially possibly to around $25 total for Michael.  If they are worried about the purpose and cost of meds, then we can determine if he''s a good candidate for MCS at that time.  He''s 55 and could be on this for a long time. Christina will call her provider and double check that the chosen Select Health plan is truly in network for her oncologist. Once she''s confident she will complete their enrollment and let me know.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-11 12:10:40', '2024-01-11 12:30:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131562021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109789002', 'Martin Smith', 'RCVD Perm. to Discuss MPB Plan with Kristina on 01.11.2024', 'Kristina, Martin''s SPOUSE, called to help Martin with his billing and sharing, since he''s in the hospital. I sent Martin the form so Kristina and the Concierge can speak freely on his behalf. First and foremost I guided Kristina to present Martin as a ''CASH-PAY'' patient to the billing department.
Presently, Martin is hoping he can just heal from here. If not, surgery is in the talks, Kristina said.
Therefore, I coached her on the need to fulfill the IUA first, collect all the receipts and invoices. Learn which direction the doctors are going: surgery OR NOT, then we can discuss how to share whatever bills sprout from this specific event. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-01-11 11:22:08', '2024-01-11 11:30:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131568003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082496017', 'Asiye Erdilek', NULL, '1/11/24: Mbr called in to inquire about the MAP program. Explained the limitations of the four visits per session and three month break in between them, guided her to our website and showed her how to access the MAP and provided her with the phone number so she can see if there''s a therapist nearby for her daughter to see. -WU', 'Willis Upton', 'Willis Upton', '2024-01-11 11:09:39', '2024-01-11 11:09:39'),
