  ('zcrm_1579374000131229044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045841172', 'Shoshana Kressler', NULL, '1-5-24 They are losing Medicaid Jan. 31st after a few years being covered. They are looking at all options including MCS, C4 and Cloud Medical. However, Sam is seeing a neurologist at BMC for neuropathy in his knee and their son has an appt with an ENT in March for some issue as well. Knowing this and the fact that they can get about a $502 APTC with $125K income, they may be best served on C4 for now until these health issues are resolved. Although, with their S-Corp, Sam has a $100K W2 income plus Shoshana has about $25K. But, I recommended they talk with their accountant since I believe they may have a much higher number. We don''t want them to get a penalty upon tax time. Her most important Drs. are Robyn Jori Sunshine Nordstrom Lane, Dr. Joshua Avram Garfein, midwife Paige Elizabeth Swales. We looked at Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0 and their cost is $817.52. However, if their income is significantly higher, we may want to re-evaluate. She will discuss it with Sam and create or login to their C4 account from many years back.  Also, she sees with Dr. Tusek at Cloud Medical they can get Zion + Cloud for only about $750 a month, she thinks. However that might be for the 18-29 age group.  They also want to review the HMA or dental discount plan. Most interested in HMA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-05 16:36:53', '2024-01-05 16:40:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131229039', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027674121', 'WAHEED AYUBI', NULL, '1-5-24 I called and left a vm to make sure they understand the pre-x clause with their babies since the mom was on some traditional ins for the maternity. Only the father was a member with MCS. Hopefully they''ll call me back.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-05 16:26:13', '2024-01-05 16:26:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131185153', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027674051', 'Michelle Searles', NULL, '01.05.2024 Michelle put in an rx request for:
Clindamycin Phosphate - 60 ML of 1 % lotion
Winlevi - 1% cream in a 60 grams tube

I sent her the following:

I am glad I was able to find you coupons for the following:
Clindamycin Phosphate - 60 ML of 1 % lotion
Winlevi - 1% cream in a 60 grams tube

The average price for Clindamycin in your area is $100.41.
The average price for Winlevi in your area is $694.64.

Below are the prices as of today 01.05.2024:
Clindamycin Phosphate - 60 ML of 1 % lotion: City Market = $24.03
Winlevi - 1% cream in a 60 grams tube: City Market = $600.60 OR Walgreens = $508.54.

Given the hefty price for Winlevi, I searched for a savings card on the manufacturing website. Unfortunately, it is only available to commercially insured individuals. Here is their verbiage: https://mprsetrial.mckesson.com/8026/
Therefore, I took the liberty and connected with our international shopper on Winlevi. I am waiting to hear back. In the meantime, attached are three coupons for your convenience to make a decision. Once I hear back from our international shopper, I''ll forward you his quote, should he be able to source Winlevi.

Lastly, the alternative pharmacy you shared, Summit Pharmacy, did not show up in any of my searches. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-01-05 16:22:45', '2024-01-05 16:22:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131185145', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128916028', 'Trevon Stoltzfus', NULL, '01.05.2024 Trevon emailed back today @ 1pm, did not see it till after our meeting (we were in a meeting that went over the hour), inquiring: "Any movement on this? I have surgery on Tuesday and need to get this issue with Zion figured out

