  ('zcrm_1579374000131096054', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021624001', 'Rachel Holden', NULL, '01.03.2024 Air lift shared? Rachel called to learn if the catastrophe that requires air lifts is shareable. I read her the guidelines straight off the internet from Zion''s website confirming any ambulance transportation is shareable, land and air. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-01-03 15:52:49', '2024-01-03 16:40:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000131097026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021624001', 'Rachel Holden', NULL, '1-3-24 Rachel called bc their neighbor''s son had to take a life flight from MT to UT for a health event which made her nervous about her membership whether or not it included this. I read the Sharing Guidelines to her: Ambulance Transport
Medical transportation, including air and ground, is eligible for sharing when it is required in relation to a specific shareable illness or injury. Every effort should be made to be transported to the closest appropriate facility.
However, she can get an additional benefit on her own for life flights for only $75 a year! So, she might just add that as an extra precaution. She said the bears are getting bad up there now and she mtn bikes in the back country often. So, you never know. 
She was super appreciative of my thoughts and the guidelines.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-03 15:39:17', '2024-01-03 15:39:17'),
