  ('zcrm_1579374000130897035', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128179061', 'Debra Sloan', NULL, 'Member called in and made me aware of the fact that she had been doubled billed for both November &amp; December pmts.  After looking into this there are 2 separate memberships created at the exact same time.  I will cancel one of the memberships and refund the 2 share amounts associated with them.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-12-29 08:04:23', '2023-12-29 08:04:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130897030', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000101104002', 'Tennison Barry II', NULL, 'Spouse called in asking about reimbursement for a "Secondary" Mammogram.  Bill came to $1100.  I advised that since this would be under the $2500 IUA that would be her responsibility.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-12-29 08:00:54', '2023-12-29 08:00:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130903003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128960002', 'Raymond Wagner', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-12-29 07:48:23', '2023-12-29 07:48:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130896013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064414873', 'Jillian Livingston', NULL, '12-28-23 Jillian called bc she got a RMHP from her local broker. However, her husband just got a new job and is offered affordable healthcare but he rejected it. Then they are getting a tax credit via C4 that they don''t qualify for since he''s offered affordable healthcare. Her broker didn''t pick up on this, so they need to address this with them. She was nervous bc her colonoscopy back in 2021 they are still paying off bc she had polyps removed and it turned to diagnostic. Since her Dr. records showed stomach pain they deemed it pre-x!  It was super brutal and she had to pay about $8K for all of it which also included an endoscopy which she just would have waited to do. She was nervous about it all and hence why they were thinking of bailing on MPB. But, they got a RMHP plan that is HSA compliant. So, she thought they''d have co-pays this time but not if it''s HSA compliant. She was making the decision quickly since it''s the holidays and is second guessing it. She will talk with her husband and may keep MPB and cancel her RMHP before Jan. 1st to get their money back.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-28 18:25:41', '2023-12-28 18:25:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130896008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130802017', 'Bruce Maleski', NULL, '12-27-23 I spoke with Sara about her son needing his tonsils out. The Dr. is booked out until Feb. So, I recommended that she calls the MPB Concierge Team and asks about getting pre-approval for his surgery to make sure they don''t find some way to deem it pre-x. I also told her to review her son''s records or ask the Dr. to make sure he considers it new. It''s only been an issue in the last 2 months well after their membership start date. She will do so. She wants to make 100% certain they will pay $2500 and the community will share the rest of the cost above that for the removal of his tonsils.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-28 17:47:56', '2023-12-28 17:47:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130896003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044650083', 'Meghan Van Vleet', NULL, '12-28-23 This is from her cancellation form and is good feedback.
What would you change about your membership?
I''m not sure how I would change this, but until I had recurring medical needs I would forget how to submit a need and have to re-learn. It also took me some time before I learned how to effectively communicate that the medial billing department should NOT bill RCI. Again, I don''t know how to do it differently, just giving some feedback. One idea: pair a new member with a more experienced member volunteer of similar demographic - in my case someone with kids of similar age, etc.
Did you receive enough education/​training to use your membership effectively?
Yes
Did you have your "Welcome Call"?
Yes
Would you Refer Anyone to MPowering Benefits? If NO, Why?
Yes, because it is an economical solution.
What does your new Healthcare Plan offer that MPowering Benefits doesn''t?
Greater ease for my soon to be college bound son who will not likely communicate effectively or collect appropriate paperwork when accessing healthcare.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-28 17:32:05', '2023-12-28 17:32:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130887008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064414873', 'Jillian Livingston', NULL, '12.28.2023 Jillian called to cancel her membership and get reimbursed for December. I transferred her to Wendy''s VM, b/c Wendy was engaged with another valued member at the time. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-12-28 15:40:11', '2023-12-28 15:40:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130846018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130059020', 'Elizabeth Wiersma', NULL, '12/28/23: Mbr called in and mentioned how she hadn''t got any welcome emails or cards, checked to make sure we had an accurate email and sent her the welcome email. I had mentioned that in her case since she had our co pay plan we would need to get her this card at which point she informed me she changed from the co pay plan to just the secure which prior notes reflected. Told her how she can present herself as cash pay in the meantime and told her the card itself at this point isn''t crucial but that she should still complete her welcome call. -WU', 'Willis Upton', 'Willis Upton', '2023-12-28 14:06:15', '2023-12-28 14:06:15'),
