Stephanie McCarter"', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-12-27 14:54:13', '2023-12-27 14:54:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130837003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128409012', 'Shawn Ford', NULL, '12/27/23: Shawn Ford called. She wanted to know what to do in certain scenarios. 
1. In case of injury or emergency, where to go. I advised that there is no network, and they can go anywhere and present as a cash pay patient. All bills related to an issue that go over 1000 IUA can be submitted to Zion.
2. Husband sees a nutritionist that does blood work and recommends supplements. I let her know that it would be out of pocket, however I''d like to double check nutritionists on the WHLD, and if any lab screenings would fall under aca.
3. We went over using Planstin card for preventive services, using the PHCS network, and that she can go out of network as long as provider will bill planstin. sending email to clarify.
4. Husband has diabetes. She wanted to know if his endocrinologists visits and insulin is covered? From what I can see on Zion & ACA, no. I advised she discuss this with her advisor as our plans are not well suited for individuals with diabetes. 
AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2023-12-27 14:51:10', '2023-12-27 14:51:10'),
