  ('zcrm_1579374000130747071', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027674121', 'WAHEED AYUBI', NULL, '12-26-23 Waheed called me with a LOT of questions. Gave him my email address and he sent me the message below. Issue for me is that I am completly ignornt of the Sedera product offering having never sold it;  I''m afraid providing the wrong info.  That said, would Wendy or Patti be better qualified to answer his questions and provide guidance?

"Hi Kirk,

I''m following up on our phone call.

The question boils down to the following. I''m currently with Sedera with a $1000 IUA at $559.97 and I would like to know what the final out the door comparable monthly premium would be with Zion.

I''d also like to know if the Sedera and Zion products are comparable or if there are any differences between them (caps on payouts, for instance).

Additionally, on Zion the Zion site, I see that they offer a "direct" and "essential" option, and they make Teladoc available as a $10 a month option, and I was wondering if that (Teladoc) is available as an option on my plan. I know I have CirrusMD, and I had Teladoc when I first signed up in late 2018 / early 2019, and was wondering if that''s available with Zion.

Finally, I was wondering if I''m able to keep the Mpowering Benefits APEC MEC HDHP plan, but drop Sedera (or Zion) altogether, so I only have the preventative coverage, but not the medical cost sharing, and if so, what the comparable premium ($559.97 being the amount I pay right now) would be.


Thanks,



--
Waheed"', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2023-12-26 12:15:00', '2023-12-26 12:15:00'),
