  ('zcrm_1579374000130516235', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000125197002', 'Richard Malcolm', NULL, '12.20.2023 Richard sent me an email asking if I can resend him the coupons I send back on 11/08. Instead I sent him the below:

I''m not able to RESEND the coupons at this time, due to the following facts:

They only last up to 7 days
The prices on these sites change DRASTICALLY, sometimes while we are in the midst of searching the medicine.

What I could do instead is to run them again and try to find the least expensive deals running, right now. I did go ahead and ping our international shopper, and I will include his quote below as well. REMEMBER if you decide to go with the international shopper''s quote, it is wise to accept that it takes time to be delivered, as it is being sent from Canada.

Attached, please find two coupons with pricing  as of today, 12.20.2023:
City Market:
Brand - Advair Diskus 100mcg/50mcg - 60 doses = $216.16
Generic - Advair Diskus 100mcg/50mcg - 60 doses = $59.64

Success! Prices went down from picking up at the pharmacy, however I did include below what our international shopper was able to conjure up, in case you are interested.

International Shopper''s Quote:
Your quotes are below. As of now we cannot source out of our usual pharmacy, due to export limits, but we can get them from other pharmacies.
Advair Diskus 100mcg/50mcg (Fluticasone/Salmeterol) - 1 x 60 dose diskuses, brand- $109.06+$9.95 (shipping)
Advair Diskus 100mcg/50mcg (Fluticasone/Salmeterol) - 60 capsules plus 2 Rotahalers, generic- $96.01+$9.95
Advair Diskus 100mcg/50mcg (Fluticasone/Salmeterol) - 2 x 60 dose diskuses, brand- $153.64+$9.95
Advair Diskus 100mcg/50mcg (Fluticasone/Salmeterol) - 120 capsules plus 4 Rotahalers, generic- $134.77+$9.95', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-12-20 16:44:32', '2023-12-20 16:44:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130516221', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000093898002', 'Matthew Hoit', NULL, '12.20.2023 Selina went for a physical on  9.28.2023. Had the standard blood work done. Planstin is billing her around $50, after covering the other parts.
Spoke with Caitlyn 3 way call with Selina at Planstin, and she shared what she was viewing on her monitor, explaining all that has been covered and how the ~$50 is part of her deductible.
I asked Caitlyn when did this begin to be, as since I started working here 1.5 years ago, any member on the Secure plan, has their preventative through Planstin with all their screenings covered 100% under the ACA guidelines.
Per my request, Caitlyn went and checked with someone who was seasoned on this matter.
She came back with that she was misreading the plan, and the $50 is the member responsibility
to meet the deductible.
checked on plan
