this guideline is on since June. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-12-20 16:15:22', '2023-12-20 16:30:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130564034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130526365', 'Isaiah Burdon', NULL, '12-20-23 Brianna called and wants to convert their brand new term life policy to an IUL with a lump sum deposit. It''s best to leave the term intact to have the same DB for both partners in the biz. We could build a new IUL and build with the smallest DB possible and highest cash value. Then this can be used for retirement purposes.
UPDATE - Brianna''s credit has some dings that she''s working to correct ASAP. But, they want to get an IUL to be able to access cash from it right away for down payment on the loan.  So, she wants to know max they can access right away as well. They have a lump sum of $30K and want to fund it from the business about $300-$500 ongoing, if all goes well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-20 16:13:51', '2023-12-20 16:33:01'),
