  ('zcrm_1579374000130444059', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121978002', 'Amelia Carter', NULL, '12-19-23 Amelia is cancelling due to some pre-x issues she has that she wants covered. She was never very thrilled to have MCS to begin with but it was offered by her employer Brent Kruehl. She''s now getting a subsidy in TX for a plan and Brent wanted to confirm, which I will do.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-19 16:30:02', '2023-12-19 16:30:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130444049', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010543087', 'Tania Dibbs', NULL, '12-19-23 Tania is still getting denied for everybody to bill to Planstin in the Aspen area, short of driving an hour. The new place she found simply says "no they won''t bill to Planstin." The place that shows Drs. in network is the same place where she had a nightmare experience last year. So, if all else fails, perhaps I can ask Planstin to help her with reimbursement for cash pay. Otherwise, if/when we have a new wellness solution she''s open to better options!  She doesn''t need this immediately but would like to make some decisions in Jan. or Feb. to get it done soon thereafter. She''s willing to wait a little for an easier solution.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-19 16:23:33', '2023-12-19 16:23:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130444044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000078638002', 'Claudia Nanino', NULL, '12-19-23 Claudia asked many questions via email and I decided to answer via phone since it was much easier to explain. She''s looking at other options and I think someone has her a little nervous. I explained the financial back up plans in case of low funds, explained IUA and no cap, explained it''s necessary for pre-approval for alternative care situations. She''s in the middle of a diagnosis and working with a functional medicine Dr. I suggested she calls the MPB Concierge Team for guidance in how to obtain pre-approval for that issue. She will do that and was very appreciative.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-19 16:02:13', '2023-12-19 16:02:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130439028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061091330', 'Krista Rogers', NULL, '12.19.2023 Krista called to confirm if an injection is shareable. According to their guidelines straight from their website on 12.19.2023, injection are:
22. Injections
Injections related to an eligible sharing request are shareable up to $5,000. Hormone therapy
injections related to an eligible sharing request are shareable up to $3,000. Injections related
to gender transitioning or sex reassignment therapy are not shareable.
Krista was transferred to Zion to speak to them directly and confirm, for good measures. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-12-19 15:47:33', '2023-12-19 15:47:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130444036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130664048', 'Caryl Wojcik', NULL, '12-19-23 Caryl''s DOB 9/29/65, Mark is 55 and 7/13/1969 and son is 22, April, 2001 and is special needs and non-binary. She''s a planner and just wants to price out her option when she retires on 9/29/2025 when she turns 60.  She watched the MCS video and is Not interested in MCS. She''s is self proclaimed very traditional! She expects to only draw off of their investment income at about $150K per year before they pull from SS. This still manages to get them an APTC of $793 in 2024, but who knows for 2025.  About 6 months into retirement they will remove their son from their plan which will again change the equation.  This gave her plans at full price about $1300 (their cost $535) for a plan I wouldn''t recommend to a Cigna Connect Bronze plan that I would recommend at $1731 (their cost $938).  This is exactly the guidance she wanted to plan out their finances for retirement to make sure she can retire. She''ll call me in early 2025.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-19 15:41:07', '2023-12-19 15:41:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130444031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000014431007', 'Suzanne Cote', NULL, '12-19-23 Suzanne talked with her new employer and they don''t have to offer benefits to part-time employees. So, she''s going to ask them not to offer her healthcare benefits. That way she can keep her APTC and current plan for only $40.88. Otherwise, she will have to accept their plan with her cost at $345 and that take half of her stipend for her new job. She''s not even sure she''ll stay with the company or if she''ll be successful since she will make most of her income off commissions. They are totally outdated in their processes and make her draw the samples of closet designs instead of doing 3D modeling like most other companies are offering now. She''s not thrilled with them and the job may be short lived. Keeping her current plan feels best to her for now. She has until tomorrow to decide and for the company to remove that benefit from her offering.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-19 15:28:15', '2023-12-19 15:28:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130439023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086967002', 'Kris DiNucci', NULL, '12.19.2023 Deandra had to go to the hospital a month ago. They misrepresented with Planstin with the hospital. I coached Kris to reverse that action, and tell the hospital that they are cash pay patients, and even request the cash pay discount.
I explained the 6 months deadline, the fulfilling the IUA, $5000 for them, and the number of IUA''s each membership is responsible for in a year.
Kris is going to speak to the hospital to correct the billing, gather all appropriate paperwork, and call us back to connect with Zion. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-12-19 15:26:28', '2023-12-19 15:26:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130399028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116120018', 'David Cole', NULL, '12/19/23: Reached back out to Dorothy to discuss what to expect when enrolling a child past the 30 day timeline but go no answer, will follow up tomorrow before 3 pm EST as it is the deadline. -WU', 'Willis Upton', 'Willis Upton', '2023-12-19 15:01:33', '2023-12-19 15:01:33'),
