  ('zcrm_1579374000130219021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130215078', 'Ashley Arman', NULL, '12-14-23 Ashley is 30 and Sean is 31, plus a 3 year old.  She wants freedom of Drs. 2 years ago their Cigna plan cost $800 which was too much and then went up to $950 for the family. Yes, they want wellness and No for HSA. Ashley has Krohn''s Disease since 17 yrs old which has been in remission for a while by changing diet, natural healing remedies, humidifier, etc. They don''t use tobacco. Ashley''s on blood pressure meds, pain pills, ADHD meds as well.  They are not good candidates for MCS since they don''t want to split up their family and Ashley doesn''t want the pre-x issue with her health stuff. Their gross income is $150K but $70,500 AGI as best guess. She didn''t want to take the APTC up front but then realized it''s the only way they can afford ins, so seemingly willing now. They chose a Cigna plan with my help that is back in their price range.  They live in Mead, CO. They also want Dr. Scott Timlin DDS at Erie or Mead Family Dentistry at 80542. They accept Aetna PPO only, not HMO or other. They accept Met Life, Delta Dental, Cigna, United Concord, UHC and PPO only for all.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-14 12:43:01', '2023-12-14 12:47:35'),
