  ('zcrm_1579374000130219011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130567002', 'Savannah Lewis', NULL, '12-14-23 Savannah is 26 or 27 and her husband is 30. She''s a new ins agent working with her mom Julie Lewis at Integrity Insurance. She and her husband are looking to get pregnant and haven''t had success yet since March. Her husband got kicked off his company ins so they don''t have anything right now (I think). She read the info I sent to Julie but will watch the video. I read from the newest Sharing Guidelines for Jan. 1st that there''s no 60 day waiting period anymore!  That''s huge for her. She will make sure by the 20th that she''s not currently pregnant and then will wait until the new year to be safe. Her husband uses tobacco and she knows of the $50 a month tobacco surcharge and limits once he reaches 50+ in 20 years. This can be incentive to quit now. I will send her the newest Guidelines and Maternity Guide. She wants to start with CARE+ and then upgrade to SECURE if/when their baby is born for the wellness aspect. She receives W2 from Integrity Ins and gets commissions as 1099 she thinks. Ideally she wants a Jan. 1st start date as long as she''s not pregnant yet.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-14 12:02:55', '2023-12-14 12:02:55'),
