  ('zcrm_1579374000130138136', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000104398007', 'Estefania Luna', NULL, '12-13-23 I completed the enrollment finally after wasting a TON of time. Anthem''s enrollment portal was missing the text to check a box to continue. The only way it worked was to login as the client with the PIN Anthem sent and proceed as the client. Then the missing text showed up and I could continue and enter the cc pmt info to be billed on the 1st of every month ongoing. Plan is $219.94 for her Catastrophic plan. I need to inform Jennifer that all 3 employees are now enrolled for 2024.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-13 17:45:04', '2023-12-13 17:45:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130142037', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124507238', 'Denise Burnett', NULL, '12-13-2023:  RX Quote:  Sent the following info.  Denise req''d Walgreens, but CVS was cheapest.  This is a super expensive item.  Reid cannot source.  She lives in a smaller town (Grand Junction, CO), so I sent her the req''d Walgreens coup, but also the cheapest = CVS (& sugg she see if the Target store has a CVS inside & would honor this. Target has a great customer rating & the stand alone CVS = 1star).  Sugg she could try Costco & Sam''s = sometimes if you have the higher memb = good RX rates we cannot see.  I could not get the coupons to save, so Nahla saved & sent them to me to fwd.
     - Botox Injectible 100 units/vial x 2 vials = $1316 at Walgreens on GoodRX
        OR  $1227.28 at CVS on Sngl Care     - CA', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-12-13 17:35:09', '2023-12-13 17:35:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130142026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012675007', 'Michelle McGimpsey', NULL, '12.13.2023 Michelle called with a hospital bill from a visit in July. Michelle also just lost her husband, recently. She needed guidance as to how to proceed to get coverage.
I walked her through the sharing request steps. I requested that she gather all her paperwork, call the hospital and request a cash pay discount, call us back to guide her through applying for the sharing request. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-12-13 16:18:13', '2023-12-13 16:24:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130142021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110552002', 'Sheryl Hadley', NULL, '12.13.2023 Sheryl was referred to call us per Wendy''s request, regarding several sharing requests. One of them being a torn tendon in one of her hands.
She basically wanted to learn how to proceed from here, so I guided her to:
1-collect all her receipts, and separate them via issue
2-add up the total cost per issue, write it on a sticky note on top of each section
3-identify if the IUA has been met per issue, if yes, call us back and we will proceed with the sharing request.
Sheryl also asked about her physical annual visit she had almost a year ago. She was unsure as to how to present in that situation, so it sounds like she''ll have to make that out of pocket. However I did ask her to call us, making us her first stop, when she''s ready for the next annual physical. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-12-13 16:14:09', '2023-12-13 16:25:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130138131', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130152006', 'Troy Baker', NULL, '12-13-23 Troy is the son of Donna Baker. Troy is 28 and just lost his job and his benefits ended Nov. 31st, 2023. So, he just enrolled in CARE+ at $1000/$240.  He doesn''t know what his next job will be or if he will get any benefits. Donna wanted to make sure it was fine if he had to move home and change his address at that time. I let her know that''s easy. He''s healthy, no pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. He watched the video. Cobra will cost $474.26, so that''s not a good option for him. He''s all set moving forward. I let him know to save the Quick Reference Guide and set his Welcome Call appt.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-13 15:48:27', '2023-12-13 15:48:27');
INSERT INTO zoho_import.notes ("note_record_id", "person_type", "person_record_id", "person_name", "note_title", "note_content", "note_owner", "created_by", "created_time", "modified_time") VALUES
  ('zcrm_1579374000130138126', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000127019002', 'Donna Baker', NULL, '12-13-23 Donna and her 28 year old son called to add him onto his own membership. He''s not employed at the moment, so CARE+ is the best. He doesn''t know what his next job will be or if they will offer benefits. He may also have to move home to the farm for a period of time depending on job prospects. He''s healthy, no pre-x, no meds, no tobacco use. Cobra will cost $474.26 if he chooses that for Dec backdating. His benefits ended Nov. 31st already.  He''s choosing CARE+ $240/$1000 for Jan. 1st 2024 start date. 
Donna also asked about possibly adding employees later down the road. I explained the only difference is in how it''s billed.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-13 15:37:26', '2023-12-13 15:37:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130138118', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011083214', 'Jesse Chatham', NULL, '12-13-23 Jesse is getting onto an ACA plan bc he''s a tobacco user and now 50+. So, he will be better protected with Bronze ACA moving forward. Julie is a photographer and self-employed so she will be the primary now moving forward and will keep the kids on this membership.  We cancelled Jesse for 12/31/23 and he did ACA on his own and doesn''t need help for now. Julie re-enrolled into SECURE HSA EC $555 for Jan. 1, 2024. I''m asking Patti to make sure they are backdated to Oct. 1st, 2021 with their original start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-13 15:14:54', '2023-12-13 15:26:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130138113', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010282133', 'Susan Atchison', NULL, '12-23-23 Apparently Planstin, Zion and MPB have no records of her calling to ask for her wellness visits to be covered. So, I don''t know who she was calling. But, I''m hoping to hear back from her today or tomorrow once she''s free. 
UPDATE - It now sounds like her Drs. office never submitted the claim and just billed her for the wellness visit. Also, supposedly, her Drs. office said it was too late to submit the bill but I don''t believe Planstin has any deadline for submission. Either way, she''s tired of dealing with it all and is getting a subsidy via ACA and is saving $300 a month.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-13 15:00:22', '2023-12-13 15:00:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130142016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129823144', 'Pam Adamson', NULL, 'Nahla is posting this for me since I do not curr have access to the CRM:
12-13-2023:  Pam called.  Lots of questions:
     - Wanted to sub all her receipts twds her IUA.  We did in depth educ on how the IUA works.  Then we discussed the diff ''issues'' that the receipts represent:
     - Mamm:  She knows Planstin ''prev'' should pay for the 2D as long as they prov bills Planstin.  IF there is an issue (say they see something & want to diagnostically test her), then it would move to her healthsharing & be subject to the 1k IUA.
     - How to present for emergencies, accidents, etc:  We went over that for everything except her ''prev care'', she will let the doctor, Urg Care, ER, ambulance, etc know:  no "ins", no card to present, ''cash-pay'', ask for ''cash-pay'' disc, if they ask for money ask if you can pay $1000 (your IUA) and have them bill you for the balance so you can "get the cash together".
     - Hosp, ER, etc:  She wanted to know which hospital(s), etc., she is allowed to go to.  I let her know we do not have a network, so that will be up to her.
     - Dermatology:  She went for her annual appt.  We disc the diff between a well ck (not part of the ACA''s MEC plan) and what happens if they find an ''issue'', & how it would move from maint (& generally is < your 1k IUA) to healthsharing if the ''issue'' will now be a qualified ''sharing req'' & > the 1k IUA.
     - Endoscopy, Stomoch ''issue'' her husband is having:  We did NOT discuss that their memb is super new & how pre-x works, talk about when he started having symptoms, etc.
        What we DID discuss:  If this is an ''issue'', we have a 6mos deadline to sub a ''sharing req'' to have the healthsharing community consider sharing the exp > their 1k IUA.
     This member is relatively new and although she''s had her MPB ''Welcome Call'', seems very iffy on understanding what she''s purch.  Didn''t under the IUA is diff than a Ded.  Didn''t really understand what does & does not qualify for sharing.  
     I recommended that her advisor Wendy Scipioni should have sent her the Zion Memb Guidelines (which will be updating 1/1/2024, so watch for our newsletter), & those will help her understand how the healthsharing works.
     We went over a lot.  Hopefully, she understands a little better.     - CA', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-12-13 14:59:42', '2023-12-13 14:59:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130142008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000076954787', 'Christopher Megroz', NULL, '12.13.2023 Christopher called to learn how to proceed after his daughter''s UTI visit and more. I explained that visits like that would be considered cash pay visits, just like adults'' coverage.
He asked about any percentage or reimbursement that go towards gym memberships, and all that we are aware of in his plan is the WHLCs, I guided him to that site.
Christopher had to reset his passcode, but is familiar with the site. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-12-13 14:39:05', '2023-12-13 14:52:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130106049', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000127019002', 'Donna Baker', NULL, '12/13/23: Donna called. She has a 26 year old son that works for her, and asked how to go about getting him his own policy, and if they could possibly add him as an employee or how that would work. I referred her to advisor, Wendy and provided phone number. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2023-12-13 14:31:30', '2023-12-13 14:31:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130138108', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110552002', 'Sheryl Hadley', NULL, '12-13-23 Sheryl needs help submitting a new need for a torn tendon in finger that she has a bunch of PT visits for. I let her know about the 6 month deadline which she didn''t know about. Some costs were before that but some within the previous 6 months as well. So, she''ll still submit the Need and get reimbursed for what she can. I gave the the MPB Concierge # to call next.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-13 14:20:23', '2023-12-13 14:20:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130138103', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011537054', 'Michael Sharpe', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation after contacting Sedera to cancel .  Wendy spoke to him and helped him fill out the cancellation.  I will process', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-12-13 13:58:58', '2023-12-13 13:58:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130138098', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000093072002', 'Richard Brodeur', NULL, 'Member called in asking when billing was and how she could possibly cancel her membership.  I told her to be in contact with Karen and I had to give contact info.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-12-13 13:51:03', '2023-12-13 13:51:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130138093', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122383002', 'David Edwards', NULL, 'Member reconsidered his Cancellation Request as he is still receiving benefit from the Hospital Bill Eraser.  I will reinstate', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-12-13 13:35:43', '2023-12-13 13:35:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130138088', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011537054', 'Michael Sharpe', NULL, '12-13-23 Michael is getting a subsidy via the ACA so he decided to cancel. I helped him through the process and he got to the confirmation page which he is printing to show proof, if need be.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-13 13:31:49', '2023-12-13 13:31:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130138083', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130113010', 'Alan Brockway', NULL, 'Member &amp; Ch $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-12-13 13:21:58', '2023-12-13 13:21:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000130138078', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026447189', 'David Naber', NULL, '12-13-23 Rebecca wants to run every scenario. She wants child psychologist, genetic testing, heart testing, Children''s Hospital, Kaiser Gold plans, possible surgery for herself, gout for Dave, generic drug for Dave, unknown drugs for Henrietta (Hatty) for ADHD, etc. Hatty is adopted and parents used drugs, so she wants to make sure anything she''s put on isn''t addictive. I narrowed it down to KP Select Gold 1500/25 for $622 or so bc it has low co-pays for much of what she wants and low coins for the rest. They are getting about a $1200 APTC as well. For school, you can only include $4K deducted for expense of private school, not the $24K she was putting in. C4 Rep Claire helped us to learn that. Tkt # CAS525271H5H6RO.  They also thought of keeping Dave on MPB but then that will lower their APTC and increase the cost of their plan for Rebecca and Hatty. So, that''s probably not going to serve them well either.  Dave also now has retinal occlusion from the covid booster affecting his eyesight! Rebecca has new hearing loss likely from the same. Rebecca will review everything further and wanted to look at all of the carriers which won''t offer her co-pays for everything she wants.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-13 13:20:41', '2023-12-13 13:20:41'),
