  ('zcrm_1579374000129872353', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130421011', 'Shane Mellin', NULL, '12-8-23 So, I replied to Shane with the following:

Good Evening Shane,

There is a bit of gray area and leeway with doctors who need to code their services as “preventative screening”. If they don''t then it will be the member''s responsibility to pay. The wellness benefit is the same for all ACA compliant insurance plans; they all abide by the same guidelines. So, the best thing to do is to ask the doctor to do only what he/she will code as preventative which will result in no cost to you the member.  



I hope this helps.  



Best,', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2023-12-08 20:39:41', '2023-12-08 20:39:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129872348', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130421011', 'Shane Mellin', NULL, '12-8-23 Sent the question to Wendy who replied with:
Hi Kirk,

There''s no easy answer to this. There''s a bit of gray area and leeway with the doctors. They need to code their services as preventative screening. If they don''t then it will be the member''s responsibility to pay. Keep in mind the wellness benefit is the same for all ACA compliant insurance plans. They abide by the same guidelines. So, the best answer is to ask the dr. to do only what he/she will code as preventative and will be at no cost to the member. 

Good luck,

Wendy Scipione', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2023-12-08 20:38:42', '2023-12-08 20:38:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129872343', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130421011', 'Shane Mellin', NULL, '12-8-23 from Shane:

Thanks for the follow up Kirk.

