  ('zcrm_1579374000129838003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122383002', 'David Edwards', NULL, '12-7-23 David is making use of Script Sourcing. His $1.7M doctor bills have now been lowered to $690K which is still unbearable. He will now be able to access VA benefits moving forward and possibly Medicaid at some point. I''m still waiting to hear from Bryan Amaya if there are any other solutions for the remaining $690K. David will be cancelling by the end of the month since there''s not much more to be done.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-07 21:26:32', '2023-12-07 21:26:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129798081', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063775002', 'Daniel Gutierrez', NULL, '12.07.2023 Hello Martha,

I profusely apologize for the time it took for me to respond. This transaction, per se, is a sensitive one. I wanted to make sure you had the education on how to use your health-sharing, once you make this change. 

Below are the details that you need to be aware of, should you need to submit a sharing request, after you make this IUA change:
You can change your IUA once per year.
There is a 60-day waiting period, from the effective date of the change to the new IUA, before it becomes active.
Any previously opened sharing requests, will have the old, higher IUA.
Any new, sharing requests opened AFTER the 60-day waiting period, will have the new lower IUA, even if the issue is in the medical records prior to the new IUA.  It is based off of the date the request is submitted..

For example:  If you submit a change of IUA on 12/19/2023, it will become effective on 1/1/2024.  Any sharing requests already submitted or submitted between 12/19/2023 and the end of the waiting period (60-days) = the old IUA.

If a new sharing request is submitted AFTER the 60-day waiting period is over = the new, lower IUA. 
Please do reach out to us if you have any questions or concerns.

Attached please find the form to submit to change your IUA. Please be sure to submit it by the 19th of this month, for the requested effective date.
https://www.cognitoforms.com/MPoweringBenefits1/MPoweringBenefitsExistingMemberChangeForm', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-12-07 17:55:48', '2023-12-07 17:55:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129798073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031672299', 'Melissa Lagassie', NULL, '12.07.2023 The below email to Karina and Patti sum up the conversation with Melissa:

Good morning Karina,

I had the pleasure of speaking with Melissa Lagassie last night. She''s in our system as active in the CRM, and inactive in Admin123.

She began her initial concern with the fact that she left her employer on November 14, and that she spoke with someone (She''s under the impression that she spoke with someone from MPB, but I''m not so sure, since there are no notes anywhere) from MPB who told her that her benefits were canceled as of August. 

I double checked the Admin123 platform and confirmed with her that is indeed the case, but not in the CRM. The last time she was charged was 7/27/2023. However, she shares that she did not receive any documentation from MPB letting her know that her benefits were cancelled, or are about to being cancelled. Furthermore, according to her, her employer continued pulling money from her account towards her benefits. 

She proceeded to ask the following questions:
"Then who is pulling money from my account?"
"Will I get reimbursed?"
"Did everyone else on that list bill get cancelled as well?"

I repeatedly responded to her and let her know, ever so gracefully, that I have not been educated on the list bills, and the people she will need to correspond with are presently gone for the day, due to the EST time zone. I offered to transfer her to your VM, but after the 3rd  time her asking me "Who is pulling money from my account?", she was not happy with my response, and hung up on me. 

Would you be so kind to reach out to her and clarify all her inquiries and concerns?

Melissa Lagassie: (860) 999-1771, THIS is the number she called from last night (860) 730-4917.

I Cc''d Patti due to the comments on being billed and needing reimbursement.', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-12-07 16:31:28', '2023-12-07 17:25:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129812016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129829002', 'James Benvenuto', NULL, '12-7-23 James called to enroll their family into SECURE HSA $1005/$1000 EF Jan. 1st start date. He''s all set! He might need my help at the beginning which is fine.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-12-07 16:28:54', '2023-12-07 16:37:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129798059', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000127964002', 'Melissa Griffith', NULL, '12.07.2023 Emailed Leslie Jablonski, the advisor he remembers signing up with. But her response back was, "thank you for the update". 
