---- on Tue, 28 Nov 2023 13:58:53 -0700 Cari Adams-Waneka<support@myahe.zohosupport.com> wrote ----
Cari Adams-Waneka      28 Nov     01:58 PM     ( responded in 5 hours )

Hi Misty,

The concierge team is working to get a new pdf Planstin ID card for Maryann.  She would have received the original card way back in September-ish of 2022.  So, it''s probably lost somewhere.  

I''m not having them send out a new hard copy card, as they are sending new cards sometime next year anyway.

Several things on the colonoscopy:

For ''preventative care'' through Planstin, they do not reimburse, so hopefully, the doctor''s office will be willing to bill for her. (Making sure the provider(s) involved will bill Planstin for you is of upmost importance for preventative care.)  Generally, since she paid instead, the patient can call the office and say, "I forgot to present my ''insurance card'', so I need to give it to you and have you bill them for me."  When using their Planstin component, it is the ONLY time they will use a card and they only time they will say, yes to having insurance.  Once the doctor''s office receives payment, they can then reimburse the patient.

NOTE: Colonoscopies often move to ''diagnostic'' (rather than a preventative screening) which makes it a healthsharing issue (with an IUA) if they pulled any polyp(s).  We can walk her thru that process if that is the case.  We always encourage members to call the concierge line proactively, so we can make sure they know guidelines of the component they are planning to utilize.  We don''t want the bad surprise of a member owing an IUA if they pull polyp(s), so please know we will guide them ahead of time.
