  ('zcrm_1579374000129141107', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000127019002', 'Donna Baker', NULL, '11-7-2023:  Donna called.  They have a plethora of RXs they want to see what pricing will be like.  Not nec needing immed, but for future info.  Told her I''d send asap.

Sent her the following (no coupons since they are not picking up curr.  They like Walmart &amp; Drug Mart.', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-11-22 20:04:13', '2023-11-22 20:04:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000129141096', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000083099001', 'julia avalon', NULL, '11-16-2023:  Sent 2nd req.  Although, I cannot find anything in my e-mail, Derrick resp''d on the 14th.  Ashlee sent me that resp.  Their description is below.  Julia knows it''s worth a try, but it''s difficult to know if it will fit into the exception category.  Might as well try though.  The ''list'' they discuss are MD options.
-------------------------------------------------------------     
"Ashlee Williams <AshleeWilliams@planstin.com>
Cari A.;
Derrick Udy <DerrickUdy@planstin.com>
Desiree Mckee <DesireeMckee@planstin.com>
​
Hi Cari,

Did you see Derrick’s replies on the 14th? See below:

Cari, there are 2 ways to approach the question of specialists on the Copay MEC. 

Our SBC’s –When our SBCs give copay amounts or other information related to specialist office visits, they reference any area listed as a specialty by the American Board of Medical Specialties. The list is here.

Basically, anything other than a PCP (Primary Care) would be considered a specialist, with a few exceptions

Exceptions include non-MD specialties

We should always note that the claim will be sent in with the CPT codes and diagnosis codes that help us understand what the patient is being seen for. 

Example:  There are times when an OB/GYN can be considered giving primary care. A lot of women will have their preventive exam done by their OB (Not considered a specialist visit in this instance)

Example:  We also do not consider Pediatricians as a specialist unless they are providing a specialty. A Pediatrician giving a well check is considered the child’s PCP. If the child is seeing a Pediatric Cardiologist, that would make it a specialist. 

Ashlee Williams
Agent Success Manager
icon 888-920-7526  icon ashleewilliams@planstin.com
icon planstin.com
-------------------------------------------------------------', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-11-22 19:48:08', '2023-11-22 19:48:08'),
