  ('zcrm_1579374000128898011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089051001', 'Patricia Smith', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat with Member Assistant', 'Visit ID : 3352 Question : Hello?', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2023-11-17 08:30:04', '2023-11-17 08:30:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128903001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089051001', 'Patricia Smith', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat missed', 'Visit ID : 3351 Question : How do I cancel my plan? I emailed info@mympb.com 3 days ago and have not gotten a response. Thanks.', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2023-11-17 08:28:13', '2023-11-17 08:28:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128876013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121310002', 'Cooper Aiken', NULL, '11.17.23: Member called about using planstin card to cover flu shot at pharmacy. According to guidelines, it should be covered. Pharmacist said card didn''t have the correct number to use for billing. Need clarification.', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2023-11-17 08:20:41', '2023-11-17 08:24:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128897008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120424002', 'Tory Erickson', NULL, 'Tori messaged me on SalesIQ needing to cancel their membership before 1/1/24, due to going on their employers Health care plan. I let him know I sent him the link to the cancellation form, along with tagging his Advisor Kori Allen in the email. I lastly let Tory know the deadline to not be billed for January''s coverage is 12/20/23. All set. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2023-11-17 08:02:11', '2023-11-17 08:02:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128894001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120424002', 'Tory Erickson', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat with Member Assistant', 'Visit ID : 3350 Question : Hello,', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2023-11-17 07:55:08', '2023-11-17 07:55:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128880003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043575482', 'Christina Brown', NULL, 'Member called in for help in filling out Childs "insurance" form.  I advised that she should have received both a digital &amp; hard card from Planstin.  She will be looking in her spam &amp; will reach out to Planstin.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-11-17 07:37:42', '2023-11-17 07:37:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128879003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123378002', 'Benjamin Brown', NULL, '11/17/23: Mrs. Brown called in asking for a mbr id to fill out some school forms for her child, transferred to Patti. -WU', 'MPBHealth Member Notification', 'MPBHealth Member Notification', '2023-11-17 07:36:50', '2023-11-17 07:36:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128876003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130140019', 'Keely Spicer', NULL, 'Sent email with quote', 'Reba Larney', 'Reba Larney', '2023-11-17 07:27:21', '2023-11-17 07:27:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128848073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129829002', 'James Benvenuto', NULL, '11-16-23 James and Jen watched the video. They are both self-employed. Jen had questions about her meds all for ADD, anxiety and depression. Meds are sertraline, Adderral, Mirtazopine and then for James occasionally Ambien for sleep. They were all generic and between $5-$20 on GoodRX. Jen really likes the idea of a Concierge Dr. locally that she is interested in using to get cancer screenings and such. Turns out the Concierge Dr. will charge $7K a year!!! James recognizes that she can just pay for her own cancer screenings and will be way ahead of the game. He''s not interested or worried about these screenings. He understands they now have out of network benefits in Aspen and to show the card and allow for the provider to reach out to Planstin to work out the pricing. He also understands they need to be their own advocates for the wellness visit. He''s 100% on board and just working to get his wife on board. Once I priced out her meds and explained the pre-x clause in a second conversation she seemed much closer to making a decision. She wanted it to be even cheaper than it is. Now it makes sense since she wanted to spend $7K on her Concierge Dr. James made it very clear to her that it doesn''t make sense to pay for that on top of SECURE, DIRECT or CARE+.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-16 22:25:34', '2023-11-16 22:25:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128848068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129829002', 'James Benvenuto', NULL, '11-13-23 James found me via Eric Cohen who is very happy with his membership. James is 55 and wife Jen is 49. They live in Aspen. Yes, they want wellness and HSA. They have a 17 yr old daughter and 16 yr old son. They are mostly very healthy other than a few anxiety and depression meds. Jen had ACL surgery from a skiing accident in Feb. 2023. I explained to her about the pre-x clause and that her knee would fall within that.  They were paying about $1200 with ACA and likely much more for 2024.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-16 22:19:15', '2023-11-16 22:19:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128848055', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128921001', 'Jenna Sezionale Basilicato', NULL, '11-16-23 Jenna came to me through Mara Simoneau. Jenna watched the video and was very excited since she feels aligned with it. She has two businesses of her own, one I Venture Beyond and Rooted in Expansion. They are natural ways of healing oneself. She wants to partner with MPB. She''s just getting started with her Rooted in Expansion and is working towards having 18 practitioners with 2 stewards. Her husband is currently on Medicaid but may get bumped off soon. She used to have an HSA with an old employer. She wants wellness but her own version of wellness with natural healing, not the ACA compliant type. When I quoted her the price for SECURE HSA it was too much for her and she thought Mara''s was cheaper. So, I realized CARE+ would suit her better and she''s pleased with that. She understands the importance of joining by Dec. 1st for the lower rates as well. She will review and we are meeting again.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-16 22:10:15', '2023-11-16 22:11:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128848044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129038011', 'Matthew Mason', NULL, '11/15 and 11/16/23 Matthew is 34 and wife is 34. He was dropped by Medicaid he thinks around Oct. 1. Acct # 1800046562 with C4. Income is est. at $73,900 for the two of them combined. His income is seasonal with 3 jobs and her is more stable with one job.  Their APTC is $185.30. That brought the Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0 Plan to about $512 or so. He wasn''t happy to pay that much still. So, I explained CARE+ to him and that brings the cost down to $420 and helps since they need to enroll for Dec. 1st. Their prices will likely go up for 2024. They could even choose the $2500 IUA for the $320 a month rate. They are healthy, no pre-x, no tobacco, no meds. It''s a good option and he''s not super worried about wellness or HSA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-16 21:52:42', '2023-11-16 22:02:17');
INSERT INTO zoho_import.notes ("note_record_id", "person_type", "person_record_id", "person_name", "note_title", "note_content", "note_owner", "created_by", "created_time", "modified_time") VALUES
  ('zcrm_1579374000128855034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081707002', 'Christina Johnson', NULL, '11.16.2023 Christina called to learn if the recommended glaucoma procedure is shareable. I thought it might be, but after consulting with Cari, Zion''s guidelines mention Cataract and not Glaucoma.
We tried to google search the difference and found:
"A black cataract is another name for Glaucoma. If someone loses his vision due to a black cataract, it becomes impossible to get the vision back."
I suggested that she speak to Zion directly to confirm its "shareability" or not. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-11-16 17:18:17', '2023-11-16 17:18:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128855029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012578137', 'Rachel Fisher Ingraham', NULL, '11.16.2023 Rachel called us again following up on ANY progress on the issues stated above.
I asked her if anyone has been in contact with her from the office, and she said no.
The notes directly above this one, states that this situation has been shared with the office, specifically Catherine in hopes that she will reach out to Analisa.
I offered Rachel, today, that I will send an email to Catherine, include her, and Cc Cari.
Rachel has been the kindest and most patient member THUS FAR, even though this has dragged for almost 2 months, she continues to be kind, respectful and understanding, but she''s shared that this has become extremely frustrating and I could hear it in her voice and low tone. ***************************************************************************************
I DID NOT send the email as stated before, as I was waiting to consult with Cari via teams. Cari did share that Rachel was given specific instructions during her initial call to the concierge line, but it doesn''t seem as though Rachel followed through on those action items.
After further investigation and  tiresome non-legible search on the EOB''s she sent, it looks like the following:
1- FOR 2021: She needs to call the doctor''s office back and request that they correct the billing in their system to show the visit was for TWO BOYS; Emerson AND ROWEN. That way Planstin can see it was TWO patients, and not reject one of them (PRESENTLY the EOB''s Emerson twice).
2- FOR 2023: We will RESUBMIT these for her to PLANSTIN, since it is a Planstin mishap, and powers to be are not stepping up. We are sending the 2023 declines for out-of-ntwk EOB to Derrick Udy.
3- FOR 2022: NOTHING can be done. She went out of network.

I called Rachel back to let her know the above, but got her VM. I left her a message, brief with with must do action items and if she can call us at 800*519*2969, we will go over those items to see if they were completed.   NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-11-16 16:53:27', '2023-11-16 17:44:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128848021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128843018', 'patrick fagan', NULL, '11-16-23 Patrick is 61 and daughter is 19 born on my DOB! He works for a trucking company and as a bulk mail carrier for the government. He is offered a UHC plan through his company that he doesn''t want. He found an Anthem plan on C4 that he wants. He thought he could get an APTC but didn''t want them to review his taxes. I let him know that since he''s offered a plan through his work he doesn''t qualify for a subsidy. He also gets $800 for health and wellness per month. His Anthem plan was going to cost him $900+.  So, I decided to explain CARE+ to him. This way he can save a bunch of money above and beyond the $520/$1000 membership fee. Andrea sent him to me. He found her via C4 and she texted him to contact me to hep with C4. He has already chosen his Anthem plan. I''ve now explained now to cancel his Anthem plan. He didn''t put in the initial payment anyhow. Now he''s all set for Dec. 1st at the lower 2023 rates for CARE+. He''s thrilled. I have to thank Andrea as well! He and his daughter are healthy, no pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. He will relay to her NOT to get pregnant for at least 60 days. :-) He has his commercial CDL and A license for his work. He''s all set!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-16 16:52:34', '2023-11-16 17:03:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128855024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084457009', 'Eugena Bring', NULL, '11.16.2023 Eugena called to understand how to present re: insurance. She was answering questions online for a mammogram appointment, it did not have the option for Planstin in the drop down menu, she was able to surpass it and move on. I did tell her to make sure she presents the Planstin card and guide them to call the number ending in ''7526 to bill Planstin. I told her to do the same thing at the colonoscopy and Physical annual. She had just finished getting a preventative well woman visit, and I reminded her that the only labwork Planstin will cover is the pap-smear culture. I urged Eugena to contact us prior to going to any of her visits for a refresh on how to present and successfully maneuver the appointment for Planstin to cover. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-11-16 16:39:51', '2023-11-16 16:39:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128855019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001881022', 'Carolyn Tabak', NULL, '11.16.2023 Crystal from Planstin called sharing that she just spoke with Carolyn Tabak, and that she is showing up as Member and Spouse in their system, instead of Member and Child.
I looked her up in both platforms; CRM and Admin123, and both show Member + Child. I consulted with Cari via teams to see where to send this information to, given our platforms show it correctly. ....', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-11-16 15:20:40', '2023-11-16 15:20:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128848013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082413161', 'Wayne Marrs', NULL, '11-16-23 Wayne''s plan was going from $731 to $1019.16!  So, we looked at other options and the Anthem Colorado Option Gold Pathway Essentials Std for $758.57 looks best by far. It''s showing his Drs. are in the network but I don''t trust it after Analisa saying the network changed. I''ve asked Wayne to call each Dr. to make 100% certain they will accept this plan. He will do so and let me know the outcome.  His DOB 8/21/69 and zip 80126. Drs. he wants are Dr. Richard Pang, Dr. Chang Huei Chen and Dr. Sameer Katyal Neer. None of the other Essentials plans showed up. Only Anthem Pathway HMO and the CO Pathway Essentials. None with the X showed up. Select Health also showed up as a back up, but they don''t look better.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-16 15:01:28', '2023-11-16 15:04:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128842142', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130311002', 'Nicole Plourde', NULL, '11-16-23 sent email.', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2023-11-16 14:13:42', '2023-11-16 14:13:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128815106', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121440002', 'Nellie Nutting', NULL, '11/16/23: Mrs. Nutting calling in to inquire about what would be covered by Planstin, showed her what would be covered through the ACA act and explained the importance of not letting her provider go beyond those. -WU', 'MPBHealth Member Notification', 'MPBHealth Member Notification', '2023-11-16 14:05:27', '2023-11-16 14:05:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128815098', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000119797010', 'Ron Porter', NULL, '11/16/23: Reached back out to the mbr once Healthcare bluebook loaded, sent her an email with the information and provided her the facilities over the phone as well. -WU', 'MPBHealth Member Notification', 'MPBHealth Member Notification', '2023-11-16 14:03:56', '2023-11-16 14:04:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128855008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000079922001', 'Pamela Luna', NULL, '11.16.2023 Bryan called re: two issues - one about Brayden, which I could not really speak to in detail, and the other re: his wife''s numbness in her thumbs...naturopathic doctor yes/no with Zion, how to proceed...
