  ('zcrm_1579374000128760042', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061561019', 'Lamm Inthavong', NULL, '11-15-23 Ivory called to help her dad Lamm navigate C4. She was getting an error message but I was able to get through it without trouble. He is a naturalized citizen. His USCIS is A23863191 and Doc # is 14495526.  Jake qualifies for Medicaid and is earning $9680 ish? Jake is still on Lamm''s income tax return since he''s a college student and working only part-time. Not sure why he qualifies for Medicaid but that what it shows and that''s what they said he''s on. So, Lamm and Lien are showing a $1547.34 APTC. I''m recommending Cigna Connect Colorado Option Silver for only $18.43 a month, $100 ded and $1000 mop. I looked up his Dr. Steven Albert Singer who is showing in the network.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-15 17:43:40', '2023-11-15 20:42:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128754046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109499017', 'Thomas Mele', NULL, '11-15-2023:  Mary''s sister Peg Maguire called inquiring about our plan.  Tupac is no longer an advisor, so I sent Peg to Kirk Bennett &amp; created an CRM lead showing Mary Mele as the referring member.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-11-15 17:40:35', '2023-11-15 17:40:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128754038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000113970002', 'Tracy Murphy', NULL, '11-15-2023:  Advisor Diane Border called.  She''s taken over this group & had questions re: mamm & colonoscopy for Tracy.  I went over in detail in ntwk, RBP, if polyp(s) pulled, etc.  Sugg all the providers involved call to conf w/Planstin prior to srvcs & to make sure they will bill for the memb.  Went to healthcare.gov & gave her timelines for mamm (2D if avail), colonoscopies & sugg they go one mo out from those guidelines.  ie: mamm = every 2 years, take it to the 25 mo to make sure no issue.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-11-15 17:33:18', '2023-11-15 17:33:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128754033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064218045', 'Eric Lipp', NULL, '11-15-2023:  William & I discussed the situation.  I''m unsure of all the details.  However, we decided to ask Eric to upload the new expenses to his old request.  Then, if the request has been closed, Zion can go over that with him.  I''m uncertain what Zion will consider maintenance, diagnostic, etc., w/something like a quadruple bipass several years ago.  So told William we will leave that up to Zion.     - CA

The member came back to William saying he wants us to talk w/Zion reg his "claim" for him.  Zion rarely will work through us due to privacy issues.  So, we can call over together, but there are a lot of issues to this one and Zion will be the only ones who can help.  

From what William''s comm, this member may not understand about maintenance.  May not understand that ''issues''/''sharing req'' are closed & have to be re-opened with a new IUA if dormant too long.  It sounds like this gentleman''s lack of understanding the difference between "trad ins" & healthsharing may be adding to the confusion.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-11-15 16:52:04', '2023-11-15 16:52:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128760034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128791002', 'Holly Hoxie', NULL, '11-14-23 Holly is 53 and John is 58. They are self-employed. They both have high blood pressure well managed by meds.  Yes, they do wellness and they prefer to fund an HSA. With C4 they would get a $925 APTC and the Cigna Connect Flex $0 is $573.52 with $9450/$18900 MOP vs $3000 with MCS. So, she is choosing SECURE HSA. Holly takes thyroid meds, levothyroxine and 3 blood pressure meds, lisinopril, hydrochloriciozide and metoprelol. She said it''s well managed, so I let her know high blood pressure is exempt from the pre-x clause. Also, no hospital visits for this.  Holly completed the enrollment for SECURE HSA $2500/$550. I gave her the newest Quick Reference Guide as well. Their income fluctuates so this won''t be dependent upon that.  She''s also not tied to any dr. at this time. She''s all set and happy. John was in the background listening as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-15 16:16:40', '2023-11-15 16:24:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128759011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000091198002', 'Robyn Hallet', NULL, '11.15.2023 Robyn called to talk to Cari re: perusing the HCBB. Cari was at lunch, and I was able to guide Robyn through HCBB. I sent her the HCBB instructions via Outlook.
Robyn asked if Zion can cover any out of pocket OBGYN visits/services, I told her they can and most likely will, as long as you''ve gone passed the $1000 IUA.
Robyn then shared that she needs to know what she needs to do to cancel the membership, due to finding a job. Cari had coerced her into staying till the end of the year, and Robyn was glad to have stayed, but wants December to be the last month. I told her to just make sure her form is in by the 19th. I guided her to the form. I assumed she spoke with Leslie already, since she''s spoken to Cari in details, however she had not. I encouraged her to speak to Leslie, her advisor, she asked why, and I pressed on the fact that the advisor wants to make sure all ends are tied and she will guide Robyn to anything that needs to be completed. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-11-15 15:52:20', '2023-11-15 15:52:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128759006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000069994428', 'Kelly Snider', NULL, '11.15.2023 Kelly learned that her husband is no longer covered, due to aging out. Kelly is calling to cancel her membership, but was inquiring as to why the sudden cancellation. I checked the CRM notes and emails, and both indicate solid communication attempts (2x) to both emails, re: the aging out process. 
I asked Kelly is she was able to speak to her advisor, Diane Border, and she said she had called her 1.5 ago, have not heard back, so she called us for extra guidance or clarification.
Kelly and Jeff both did not receive those emails, and are surprised since they have used our services extensively, and do receive our business emails. They are going to try to search deeper into their emails. She asked would that have been the only way they would send out that information, and I did not have an answer to that, but told her that I''ll send a message to billing (or whatever party responsible at this point).
I also recommended that she call us back to tomorrow to try to reach billing re: the cancellation and the continued unneeded membership for Kelly, in hopes for some clarification on the miscommunication tech glitch.
Kelly mentioned that she did not need this membership, but got on with her husband. Now that her husband has aged out, she wished she had received the communication to cancel right away, since she has had insurance through her job. I told her I would document the bullets we discussed, and share it with her via CRM email. I will also message billing and contact Diane Border, for a heads up on the concern. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-11-15 15:26:42', '2023-11-15 16:06:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128760023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108399027', 'Doris Medina', NULL, '11-15-23 Pushed account through with same income for 2024 to see if there are any plans with decent price for chiropractic care. She says it''s $175 now with her current plan. That''s insane! APTC is showing $1938.21!  I looked at her same plan for 2024 and it''s showing $0 charge for chiro for up to 20 visits per year with restrictions. The cash price would be way cheaper than $175 per visit. Not sure if that''s accurate.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-15 15:13:21', '2023-11-15 15:24:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128760018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128347002', 'Vanessa Stone', NULL, '11-15-23 Left vm for Vanessa for our appt right now to review life ins.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-15 15:03:37', '2023-11-15 15:03:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128760013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128347002', 'Vanessa Stone', NULL, '11-8-23 Vanessa enrolled in SECURE HSA $1000/$300. Income is $78K. No meds, no health issues, excellent credit. Debts are cc with $3500, car $13K and student loan $130K. She wants a plan close to $25 since that''s what Hope Institute will pay.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-15 14:51:01', '2023-11-15 14:51:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128785003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064218045', 'Eric Lipp', NULL, '11/15/23: Called mbr back to try and explain how he might want to submit another sharing request through zion and potentially talk to their sharing department to discuss the urgency as he needs ekg by Friday. Mbr asked us to speak on behalf of zion for him and mentions we''ve done it in the past and asks if we can resolve this for him. Told him I would look into it and see if I or someone else can call back.', 'MPBHealth Member Notification', 'MPBHealth Member Notification', '2023-11-15 14:13:03', '2023-11-15 14:13:03'),
