  ('zcrm_1579374000128493081', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128526002', 'Barbara Lucille', NULL, '11-10-23 Enrolled in Secure HSA $1000 IUA. She smokes and clicked yes.', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2023-11-10 16:46:53', '2023-11-10 16:46:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128488080', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128916020', 'Margaret Garrido', NULL, '11-10-23 Meg is 57 and her partner is 54. They aren''t married but live together. She deciding whether or not to include him on the membership.  He apparently qualifies for Medicaid though.  I gave her pricing for both on SECURE HSA. She came via Jess Muniz. She wants to fund the HSA and will get her wellness done at a traditional place since Jess practices at Holistica Health (name ?) and they don''t appear to accept ins.  Meg only has scoriasis and herpes meds, no other pre-x to worry about and partner doesn''t have anything. She is self-employed.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-10 16:43:18', '2023-11-10 16:43:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128491037', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061091330', 'Krista Rogers', NULL, '11.10.2023 Krista called to see if any therapeutic treatments are shareable. She shared that she already has a sharing request open, which is perfect, so she can now offer Zion the treatment plan to abide by the guidelines of 35 treatments or $7500 worth of sessions. Krista also asked if they would cover another practitioner''s services, also the knee area (same sharing request), and I guided her to request the verbiage to be differentiated on the treatment plans that she can submit to Zion, in order to help them understand the purpose of both.
I opened the guidelines straight from Zion''s website as I always do, to read out loud the part on therapeutic treatments to Krista, as I usually do with each member, when they ask guidelines questions.. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-11-10 16:37:12', '2023-11-10 16:37:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128488075', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128515001', 'Autumn Romero', NULL, '11-10-23 Autumn, 24 is Christine and Louis Romero''s daughter.  She''s now paying her own taxes and has her own self-employment jobs. She''s a 24 Hour Fitness Trainer and trains a client on her own as well. She''s not offered any benefits since it''s not FT. Autumn guessed her income at $22K and her APTC is $325.48 which is more than the cost of the silver plan.  So, she doesn''t have to submit payment information or anything. Her enrollment is complete and good to go per the above information.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-10 16:36:25', '2023-11-10 16:36:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128495016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012594002', 'Guy Ralfe', NULL, '11-10-2023:  tt Advisor Andrea Hinman.  The members are all set &amp; Andrea appreciated my following-up with her.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-11-10 16:27:52', '2023-11-10 16:27:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128495011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000096330001', 'Paul Lewandosky', NULL, '11-10-2023:  Lisa called back.  IF I''m understanding, she feels she''s being charged for something that ought to have been cancelled.  I trans''d her to Patti''s line since she does the cancellations.  She''ll LM if she doesn''t catch her.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-11-10 16:25:08', '2023-11-10 16:25:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128488067', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000013590075', 'Jason Adams', NULL, '11-10-23 Dawne wants ths MEC. I asked Patti how to handle it and she said we can just add the MEC via the Change Form. I looked up the price and it''s showing $636 vs $650 on SECURE. So, instead of moving them to SECURE, we are leaving them on MPB CareZ Worksite Bridge with the MEC. She''s wanting to fund the HSA as well and will ask her accountant if she can fund it fully or only 1/12 for one month in 2023. She''s all set.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-10 16:17:31', '2023-11-10 16:17:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128491032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123060002', 'Stephen Zens', NULL, '11.10.2023 Karen messaged us re: her member/preventative/coverage/EOB...
Cari requested that I call her back and give her some guidance.
I called Karen back, and she right away asked "isn''t the colonoscopies considered covered preventative, under the Secure plan with Planstin?" - I said yes, unless they find polyps and it becomes diagnostic, then Zion will kick in.
She shared that he told her that someone recommended he call Zion directly, and he did to inquire about all of this, and they sold him a separate plan for an extra $40/month. Christine is going to call them directly and have a word with them re: selling products that members ALREADY HAVE.
