  ('zcrm_1579374000128315013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130043002', 'Jonathon Waunch', NULL, '11-8-23 my answer:  Hi Jonathon,

No, it does not.  The IUA amount you pay at the hospital/Urgent Care/Doc''s office for an event, is part of your out of pocket expense on an annual basis.

So...you''d be looking at:

$665/month for membership

PLUS

Any out-of-pocket IUAs you pay for events (if you/family are having a bad year and with emergencies)

PLUS

Any office visit charges you incur outside of the MEC (Minimum Essential Coverage) items.  The Secure HSA plan does cover all those wellness etc visit. 

Great questions, hit me with more as they come up.

Best,

Kirk', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2023-11-08 11:18:24', '2023-11-08 11:18:24'),
