  ('zcrm_1579374000128301003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000088078001', 'Nathaniel Grabau', NULL, '11-8-23 Nathan called in to add his wife Zoe, 22 to the membership. They''ve been married for a year and a half already. She''s still been on her parent''s ins not knowing she shouldn''t be. I explained CARE+ to her from start to finish and it gave Nathan a refresher. They asked about Maternity and I let them know about the 60 day waiting period and I will send the Maternity Guide and the Welcome Call invite to get her set up on virtual healthcare.  Zoe takes duloxetine for anti-anxiety which looks affordable on GoodRX and likely better pricing through another partner. Also, she takes Vienva as birth control and that looks affordable as well around $10-$15. They are good with all of that. Nathan can show proof of self-employment if need be if they want to upgrade when they have a baby sometime down the road for the wellness visits, immunizations, etc.  They know their membership will be $395/$1000 ES and will increase to $425 on the Sept. 20th billing for Oct. membership. They are happy with everything and asked a little about the Life Care. Perhaps they will use that now as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-11-08 09:41:37', '2023-11-08 09:42:39'),
