  ('zcrm_1579374000128233057', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109742001', 'Abigail Chan', NULL, '11.07.2023 Abigail called inquiring about getting coverage for a psychiatrist, for an evaluation and to get on medication. I learned that she is seeing a therapist through our MSEAP program, but needs to visit a psychiatrist to process the evaluation and attain a prescription.
I confirmed with her that it is cash-pay visit, but we can help with the prescription. I suggested that she just call us when she has the medication, and we will look for a coupon deal of at least 75% off, if not, the international shopper would be our next stop. I did explain the time sensitivity to adhere to in getting the mail-in order delivered. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-11-07 15:58:02', '2023-11-07 15:58:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000128233046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124141002', 'Holli McCormick', NULL, '11.07.2023 Holli called back about a few items:
1- The WW visit that she went to. They doctor would not call Planstin to bill them, claiming that this is the THIRD office she has worked with, where Planstin WOULD NOT PAY. So, she is not willing to bill them. They gave her a form to fill out to give to Planstin, but she already paid the $250. I told her, we cannot force the doctor to bill Planstin. I checked if the doctor is at least on the PHCS list, Dr. Carla Morrow in Fort Worth Texas, and she was. As a matter of fact, she was the first one that shows up. SO - I offered Holli the following trouble shooting round about way, to get the doctor to bill Planstin: WILL CONSULT Cari to attain a POC to connect with the provider''s office to persuade billing, ESPECIALLY if the doctor and the office IS ALREADY on the list.
2- Holli asked about an insurance card to give to her therapist, but I explained to her that the only insurance she has is PREVENTATIVE with Planstin. The mental therapy falls under the extra miscellaneous items under Essentials. I learned that her doctor was not on the list with MSEAP, and that her doctor was making an exception to see her under the EAP program. I inquired if she can speak with M&S to see if she can nominate that doctor, so they can add her to their list, so she can get paid. Holli will do that and get back with us. Initially I had asked if she can offer her the MPB card, to show her the ID# that proves what type of plan she has with us and all the services, but she told me that TWICE she has not received the card. She did find her ID in her portal, and will use that and explain to the therapist how her mental health program works.
3- Regarding the MPB card: I will be emailing both Kelly and Holli, requesting her fulfillment package with the MPB card, for the 3rd time. 
*****************************************************************************************
After consulting with Cari via teams, here are some directions we offered Holli:
1- ask the doctor if they are still on the PHCS network.
2- If they say, "oh no, we are no longer on there" (which can happen, and someone did not remove them). we can try the first idea that you and I discussed, in connecting them with someone at Planstin.
We covered quite a few details, if I missed anything, please let me know. We are here 12-8 EST ?.                                 NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-11-07 15:24:06', '2023-11-07 16:33:22'),
