----------------------------------------------------
From: Cari A. <cari@mympb.com>
Sent: Tuesday, November 7, 2023 12:35 AM
To: Proton Mail <designed4nothing@protonmail.com>
Cc: lesliejablonski@hsaforamerica.com <lesliejablonski@hsaforamerica.com>
Subject: Re: Membership for 2024
 
Hi Andrew,

I''m sorry to hear you are dissatisfied with your membership through MPB.  I would recommend discussing this with your advisor Leslie Jablonski.  Here is her phone number:  1-800-913-2776  and I''ve cc''d her on this e-mail so she knows of your request.

Please remember, MPB adds the following as part of your membership:
     - 24/7/365 text first telehealth where you can access a board-certified physician in around 60-seconds.

     - Life Care through our MAP (Membership Assistance Program) that provides many services, including up to 12 counseling sessions within their network in a pattern shown to help change behavior.  This component gives you access to many items including resources for legal forms, debt and purchase calculators, mental health, caring for yourself and family members, just to mention a few.  They offer webinars, self-assessments, articles, and you also receive unlimited access and utilization of their four unique mental health apps to assist you and your therapist in personal growth, depression and anxiety, substance abuse, and sexual compulsivity.

     - Prescription Best Pricing: Our team will search a minimum of 6 (& up to15) discount sites to find the best local pricing for you.  We also have an international shopper that can source many expensive items worldwide, at FDA approved pharmacies to help lower any pharmacy expenses.

     - The MPB Health Concierge: is available from 9am - 8pm  M-F at 1-800-519-2969 to help you best utilize your healthcare components.  We can walk you through which component will help you with your current need, whether that''s the preventative care on your membership, a catastrophic need, or just looking for a highest quality, fair priced provider in your area.  We often help people know how to best get their current healthcare needs met, what to expect, and when appropriate, we can try to help represent you with the various components (including giving you a voice with Zion if there is an issue -or- giving you a better understanding if they are denying a benefit you believe should be shared.  You have someone representing you, rather than the company.)
These are a few of the most utilized services that are included in your MPB Membership.  Leslie should be able to go through your benefits with you as well.

If you decide to move forward with cancelling your MPB Membership, Leslie will be able to help you through that process.  Be aware this will be time sensitive.  The two of you will need to process the cancellation before Friday, November 17th to meet the deadline for changes or cancellations to your membership for a December 1st cancellation date and to stop the November draw for your December contribution.  

Please let us know if you have further questions, but I think your advisor should be able to help you make the best decision for your situation.

Respectfully yours,

Cari Adams-Waneka
MPB Health Concierge
1-800-519-2969
