From: Cari A. <cari@mympb.com>
Sent: Tuesday, October 31, 2023 5:25 PM
To: Robin Rudy <rudyhouse22@hotmail.com>
Subject: Re: Quick question
 
Hi Robin,

Preventative care is not reimbursable.  Remember all items billed must be covered ''preventative'' care* & medically coded as such.  Labs require a completely different process.  Please call the concierge line for those details.**

Let the providers office know you are allowed to use in or out of network providers, but they must be willing to bill for you.  Then ask if they are willing to call Planstin (their phone number is on the front of your Planstin card) to see if their office is able to bill Planstin for you even though they are outside of the network (& confirm all entities involved will too.  ie:  for mammograms both the imaging and reading providers must be willing to bill Planstin for you.)

If the office is willing to call & bill Planstin for you, even though they are outside of the network, you can utilize that provider and the office should be paid for the eligible ''preventative care'' services.  

Here''s the government''s site, listing what they allow (note, only the items listed on the 3 hyperlink sites are included):

          * ​Preventive health services | HealthCare.gov
          Preventive health services
          Most health plans must cover a set of preventive services like shots and screening tests at no cost to 
          you. This includes Marketplace private insurance plans.
          www.healthcare.gov

If they aren''t willing to call Planstin or refuse to bill for you, they are not a good option.  Then, the only option if you utilize them for ''preventative screenings'' is to pay out-of-pocket.

Should it be a diagnostic appointment, it''s handled in a very different manner and most of what is discussed above is invalid.

I hope that makes sense.  If you have further questions, please call the concierge line.  Our most experienced concierge team members currently work 12pm-8pm eastern  M-F  1-800-519-2969.

Respectfully yours,

Cari Adams-Waneka
MPB Health Concierge
1-800-519-2969
