  ('zcrm_1579374000127450021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110792001', 'Donna Cox', NULL, '10.27.2023 Ted returned my call from yesterday re: the very expensive drug he put in a request for, Dupixent. I had tried our international shopper, but no luck, it was more expensive there (for the first time).
I consulted with Cari, given her pharmaceutical background, via teams, and she shared a process (below) that might help Ted attain coverage/assistance with this very expensive drug via the manufacturer. 
Ted was glad he had an option outside paying $4k, and is reaching out to his advisor per our coaching. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-10-27 12:22:53', '2023-10-27 12:22:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000127454008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000097264002', 'Marilyn Negley', NULL, '10-27-2023:  John LM for us at 9:34pm eastern last night.  He says he went to the portal & only sees his wife & one son, so he''s really freaking out.  I called & tt John.  Turns out he''s in his wife''s CirrusMD acct.
     - MPB.Health Memb Port:  showed him how to get in here so he can see everyone is listed.  He will need to remove one of his kids, but wasn''t able to do it right now.
     - Planstin:  He''s having his annual visit for ''prev care'' so we went over how to present & he found his Planstin pdf ID card in his e-mail.  His doc is not listed in the PHCS search, but I went over IF doc willing to bill for him, he can select outside of ntwk.  Told him to make sure doc''s off calls ahead of time, because if they won''t bill for him, it''s not cov.  He''s been paying for this out-of-pkt, so he may go that route anyway.
     - CirrusMD:  Let him know all adults on the membership are req''d for privacy to have their own memb w/unique e-mail address.  We got busy talking about the above & did not revisit.  It sounds like we may have to adjust everything if his wife & minor son are on his e-mail address.  He''s planning to call back anyway, so we can go over this then too.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-10-27 12:22:46', '2023-10-27 12:22:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000127453041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064410489', 'Michael DePaso', NULL, '10-27-23 Mike changed his IUA to $5000 a while back when the price increased.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-10-27 12:08:26', '2023-10-27 12:08:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000127453031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064410489', 'Michael DePaso', NULL, '10-27-23  I sent this to Zion - I''ve been speaking with Michael DePaso who referred his son Spencer DePaso to MPB and me for membership. He believed Spencer enrolled through MPB. However, I''m not certain what happened. We think Spencer enrolled about Jan. 1st of 2023 or near there. Spencer has proof of enrollment from Zion. I think he accidentally enrolled directly with Zion and not MPB. However, when he called Zion recently, from my understanding, they referred him back to MPB for assistance with a new Need. I''d love to get his membership corrected and connected with MPB properly, here on out.  Please let me know how we can resolve this.

They need significant help from me and our services. His son had a recent ER visit due to a health scare. It turns out after testing, he was newly diagnosed with diabetes and may require insulin. I educated Michael that insulin will be considered a maintenance medication and not shared ongoing. However, the ER visit, testing, etc. for the new diagnosis should be shareable. They are in a bit of a panic since that''s not what they were told by Zion. I suspect there is simply some miscommunication and misunderstanding.

Could you please help me get his membership properly connected with MPB and confirm that an ER visit for this scenario will be shareable if/when they exceed his $5K IUA. They have Not created the new Need yet, since it''s only a few days old. Michael is also threatening bringing it to a lawyer, to BBB and writing a terrible review if it''s not handled well. Just FYI. I believe this will get resolved without any of that. He seems like a reasonable guy.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-10-27 12:05:56', '2023-10-27 12:05:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000127450016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122122001', 'Elizabeth Bay', NULL, '10.27.2023 Elizabeth wanted to learn how to proceed at her non preventative appointment on monday re: her breathing/chest/asthma...
