  ('zcrm_1579374000127297023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130526392', 'Brianna Krampetz', NULL, '10-25-23 Brianna was referred to me via Kirk Bennett for life insurance. She and her boyfriend are looking to get an SBA loan of $400K for a small business and they have to show proof of life insurance to qualify. She ultimately wants life ins with cash value but for now can only afford term life to appease the SBA. She did a bunch of reasearch on her own about ins options. She also got a quote from Trans America but proceeded to find many terrible, one start reviews. Trans America was quoted at Preferred Plus for $23 a month for 15 yrs but was supposed to be for 20 years. The face amount was for $780K, but she wants a quote at $1M.  She''s healthy, no tobacco, no meds. Only health issue in family is her dad is diabetic and has high blood pressure or high cholesterol. Her mom takes an anti-depressant. Her credit score is 670.  Home loan is $260K and equity is $83K. Looks like income is $35-$40K. She also has $3K in car lease done in Feb. and $5K cc debt.  She also wants to see the cost for her boyfriend Isaiah, 2/23/91, same zip code, $60K income, $7K cc debt and splitting the mortgage and car loans.  He''s a mechanic and they go to the gym 4-5 days a week. He does have asthma which he hasn''t been hospitalized and takes anti-anxiety meds but definitely never suicidal per my questioning.  She wants me to run it for $1M and $1.5M for him.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-10-25 23:21:53', '2023-10-25 23:35:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000127297013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000127719002', 'Amber Ramirez', NULL, '10-25-23 New employee of The Hope Institute. Dec. 1st start date is the target. Healthy, sees psychiatrist and takes meds for mental health.  No tobacco. Income is $32K and possible debt soon with a car loan. DOB 7/17/89 and zip 85226. Explained SECURE and she''s very impressed by the benefits they are offering. She wants dental and vision (assuming they are offering it.) I need to double check.  She might have a life ins policy but wasn''t sure. I explained Living Benefits to her and I''ll run the numbers before our next meeting.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-10-25 22:35:58', '2023-10-25 22:35:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000127301055', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108674016', 'Thomas Langworthy', NULL, '10-25-2023:  Tom called &amp; LM.  He wanted to make sure his chg of pymt was accepted because he hadn''t seen him draw this mo.  I called back &amp; LM: we had system issues this mo, so the draw actually went thru today (you should see it in the next few days).  Also, gave him last 4 #s of the acct: 7608, we show as active so he can confirm the pymt chg is accurate.  Let him know if he has further questions, please give us a call.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-10-25 17:59:58', '2023-10-25 17:59:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000127301047', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000055626044', 'James Young', NULL, '10-25-2023:  Julie called.  Lots of questions:
     - daughter IUD:  We went over that the ''prev care'' w/Planstin will cover some IUDs, but that Planstin would have to tell her if the type they are looking at inserting is elig.
     - daughter''s prev:  The doc''s off charged them, not for prev, but because she was a new pt.  During gathering history, they went over her past menstrual issues = now not ''prev''.  She was frustrated.  We both agree this was wrong of the office.
     - If not seeing doc w/''Planstin'' prev care card on file for non-prev:  tell office Planstin not valid today.  Generally, ''cash-pay'' on those is cheaper than ntwk disc.
     - Julie''s mamm:  Julie has dense breasts & doc said she''s going to do a dense breast mamm.  But, when she read the order, it didn''t depict anything but a std mamm.  She''s going to call the center to conf what type & will make sure they will bill Planstin for their srvcs & any comp that is reading the images.  IF they only do 3D mamm, she''ll call Planstin to ask for conf (for the doc''s off) that it will be cov via e-mail.
     - Derm appt:  Gen skin ck, but she always has things frozen off.  Went over skin maint & cks = not considered ''prev care''.  IF however, it moves to a biopsy & then on of the expensive removal procedures, it could move to healthsharing.  She''d be resp for 1k IUA, and if > might be shared.  Discussed if diff body locations, could mean > 1 IUA too.
     - Wisdom teeth:  Not considered medical or ''prev care''.  Let her know her advisor Wendy may have a disc prod she offers that might help.
     - Went over most dental & vision is not part of plan, but in certain medical instances it can move to the healthsharing component.  ie: cataract surg = 1 yr waiting period (which they already passed), but 2 eyes = 2 IUAs, etc.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-10-25 17:27:13', '2023-10-25 18:15:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000127294023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061021001', 'Nathan Schultz', NULL, '10.25.2023 Maya called to attain her Planstin card while she was at the doctor''s office with her daughter. We called Planstin together, and had them send over a virtual one for her to use. THEY did not have HER email on file, so I will speak to Patti, since WE DO have it on file.
She received the card, and also sent in an RX request for her daughter''s medication. Here''s what I sent her:
