I responded to his advisor, Traci McCoid, letting her know it''s taken care of & giving her an idea of how it works for future reference as well:

02:32 PM
Hi Traci,

Nahla was able to talk with Zachary*.  Just so you know for the future:
     All adults, 18 & over, must have a separate account, under a unique e-mail address on CirrusMD.  
     Whether it''s husband, wife, adult children, for privacy concerns, they cannot be added to each other''s 
     accounts as dependants.  Children under 18 years old, can be added to both parents'' accounts though.

* It turns out both Zachary & his wife already had accounts, so Nahla helped them recognize that and gave them instructions on how to get into the accounts.  If they have further questions, she left it that they will call the concierge line again for further assistance.

If you have further concerns, please let Nahla or me know.

Respectfully yours,

Cari Adams-Waneka
MPB Health Concierge
1-800-519-2969

