  ('zcrm_1579374000126824131', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130311002', 'Nicole Plourde', NULL, '10-18-23 She''s at Target with the kids.  Her DPC will charge $180/mo. On top of our DPC charge of $660,  she''d be at $840/mo.  Told her this is still WAY lower than traditional insurance. She likes the DPC idea because she lives in a remote part of Maine and docs are hard to find. I told her that Telehealth is a great equalizer for that and she''s not a doctor-happy person...rarely goes. Wants me to call back in 2 weeks.

Sent her this from my email:
Hi Nicole,

Some thoughts for you on the healthcare front...

First, $660 for our Direct membership (at the $1000 IUA level) plus your DPC estimated rate of $180 means a total monthly of $840. I know you are aware that this is still a LOT less than traditional medical insurance.

Knowing this and since you stated you are not one of these people that is visiting the doctor every week, consider the Telehealth we provide. Statistically Telehealth handles 80% of the reasons that people traditionally visited a doctor for. This aspect can/could reduce the stress of needing a doc quickly when they''re only a phone call away, 24 hours a day. And, it''s always a doctor that you''ll be speaking with.

It''s possible this could eliminate the need for a DPC relationship. However, I don''t live in Maine and appreciate the availability (or not) of physicians in your area.

If you opted to not go with a DPC, the overall monthly will go down. We have other plans for you to look at in that case; Secure and Care+.

Secure at $1000 IUA will run you $715/mo
Care+ at $1000 IUA will run you $580/mo

Lastly, as I mentioned, you can give it a try to see...our membership is month to month so you modify or terminate anytime.

I''ll check back in a few weeks and your call is welcome anytime. 

Best,

Kirk', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2023-10-18 10:43:33', '2023-10-18 11:11:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000126836003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000126948009', 'Audrey Byram', NULL, 'Transferred over to Wendy - JA', 'Julia Avalon', 'Julia Avalon', '2023-10-18 10:42:16', '2023-10-18 10:42:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000126834008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000126948009', 'Audrey Byram', NULL, '10-18-23 Left vm for Audrey to help her with questions.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-10-18 10:39:52', '2023-10-18 10:39:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000126833008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124104002', 'Sherwin Miguel', NULL, '10.17.2023 Sherwin called. They have a pediatrician visit tomorrow - 4 months old - Dr is naturopathic - tomorrow will be a 4 month check-up & they might get an immunization shot for Kailani.
Sherwin wanted to know how to proceed, after sharing they have only been paying cash pay visits with this doctor in the past.
I offered two steps, starting with calling the doctor (assuming he/she is medically licensed), to confirm they want to do business this way, by calling Planstin to collaborate pricing and billing, THEN call Planstin (assuming the doctor is ok with the process), and confirm it is ok to proceed with THIS doctor, given that he/she is a nontraditional doctor. 
*****************************************************************************************
Sherwin called back after speaking to his doctor, to share that all they do is generate a superbill.
After consulting with Cari, via teams, I shared with him that would work perfectly, if they can go ahead and fax that straight to Planstin with the fax number on the card.
