  ('zcrm_1579374000126608024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011537054', 'Michael Sharpe', NULL, '10-16-23 I sent this to Michael with the new pricing options if he still has DPC.  I confirmed the pricing with Patti.
____
Thanks for reaching out. Do you still have your Direct Primary Care (DPC) membership?  If so, your new monthly membership contribution would change from the quoted $523.78 with your current $500 IUA to $449.78 at the $1000 IUA, $430.78 at the $1500 IUA, $416.78 at the $2500 IUA or $407.78 at the $5000 IUA. Keep in mind the IUA is the Initial Unshared Amount that you are responsible to pay first before cost sharing begins. You are responsible for up to 3 Needs or IUA''s per year, if you have that many incidents. So, it could be $5000 x 3 = $15,000, if you choose the highest IUA and had a terrible year with 3 separate medical incidences. 

I''d say the $1000 IUA level is the sweet spot. Let me know what you choose or if you no longer have a membership with your local DPC. I will help you complete the change form. We need to do this before Oct. 20th before billing takes place.

Thanks,

Wendy Scipione', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-10-16 13:53:09', '2023-10-16 13:53:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000126606087', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000055816343', 'Mary Ann Harpenau', 'This grandfathered plan is basically the ''Direct'' plan re: prev & healthsharing per disc w/Joan', '10-16-2023:  Mary Ann called for a boatload of stuff.  She tt Joan & wanted to know about the various components of her plan, so Joan told her to call the concierge line.  Her plan is super old & I need to conf w/Joan, so sent Joan a Teams chat request for us to talk later today.  Mary Ann has an appt w/Joan tomorrow, so this way, when she tt Joan then, they can conclude the following:
     - CirrusMD:  We were able to get Mary Ann all setup under her e-mail: mharpenau@msn.com & an invitation has been  sent to her husband Jaime w/his: awprotection@gmail.com
     - Wants to see online a list of her benefits.  This old plan looks like our current Direct Plan after Joan & I dug into it.  I gave Mary Ann, Joan''s replicated website: joinmympb.com/joan & told her Joan will confirm which curr plan is most similar so she can look at her benefits online (as we do not have old listings of the grandfathered plans).  I let her know this will basically be what she currently has.  [The one diff, which I did not mention:  She will need us to work up anything in HCBB as this eff date time period does not have access to do things themselves.]
