  ('zcrm_1579374000126577003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109781008', 'Lauren Guida', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation eff 11/1  request due to the fact that she will be leaving the country for an extended period of time.  I will process and cancel any further billing.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-10-16 07:30:55', '2023-10-16 07:30:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000126554034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000084517001', 'Kyle King', NULL, '10/15/2023:  Kyle e-mailed wanting to find out if Covid & influenza shots are covered.  We finally got written confirmation that Planstin will pay for Covid shots & boosters, so I sent her the information and included the healthcare.gov link.  There are no participating pharmacies within 20-miles of her zip code:
     There are two ways to take advantage of getting your immunizations:
     - Your doctor can give you your immunization(s) at the office and as long as they will bill Planstin for you, both the immunization(s) and visit will be paid for.  
        Your plan allows you the best of both worlds: you can utilize the PHCS Network of doctors or choose your own doctor as long as they are licensed and willing to bill Planstin directly for you.
     - The other option is a pharmacy that is willing to bill Planstin for you.  Planstin''s phone number is on their card.  If the pharmacist has questions, they should be able to call Planstin for billing instructions.
Covid shots still have government funding available in most areas.  

     If nothing above works for your situation, let the pharmacy know you do not have insurance for your Covid shot or booster and they should be able to bill the government for you.

     ** NOTE:  The RSV vaccination is not yet covered by your ''preventative care''.**

Please let me know if you have further questions.  This can be very confusing, so don''t hesitate to call the concierge line (best to call between 12pm-8pm eastern time for the most experienced staff: 1-800-519-2969  ext #:2).', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-10-15 00:33:23', '2023-10-15 00:33:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000126556018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011521660', 'Teresa Robertson', NULL, '10-13-23 Teresa called Zion to understand how to complete her wellness visit and they told her to pay cash and bill to Zion. Then Zion later told her to bill it to Planstin. She asked the provider to re-bill it to Planstin now which they agreed to do. The bill was about $193 plus $160 for labs. The labs will re-bill as well. She was super frustrated by getting wrong info from Zion and getting passed back and forth between the two. This makes her super nervous for bigger issues, if this is the way it goes. I let her know next time it''s best to contact the MPB Concierge Team for the best assistance. We will wait to see if it progresses forward. She submitted the super bill now to Planstin. If she doesn''t hear anything in a week or so, she''ll contact me and I''ll forward it along myself before we lose her as a member.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-10-13 17:58:35', '2023-10-13 17:58:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000126551041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000119626010', 'Alicia Koscinski', NULL, '10.13.2023 Left a VM for Alicia, regarding the above request. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-10-13 17:53:14', '2023-10-13 17:54:49'),
