  ('zcrm_1579374000126176155', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080099002', 'Michelle Stevens', NULL, '10-9-2023:  CARI DOES NOT HAVE ACCESS TO THE CRM. Here are her notes:

Michelle called.  Her 19 yr old daughter is having eating disorder issues.  The school counselor has diagnosed her w/anorexia and wants her to see a nutritionist.  We realized she''s having trouble getting into her Zion Memb Portal, but was requesting a pw reset while we talked.  She will see if she can get in to submit items twds her daughter''s eating issue.  She knows, although they do have benefits listed in the Zion Guidelines for the nutritionist, that the counselor to get to that point may or may NOT have impact.  We decided to sub the sharing request under "Nutritionist" and maybe the counseling will count twds her IUA.  She knows it is a long shot, but at least she will have tried.  She''s going to get it all together & we walked thru her options for how to sub the ''sharing req''.

     - If she can get into her portal, she will look for the ''sub sharing req'' link & follow their instructions.  Because she''s had trouble w/this before I did not go over anything here.  She''ll call if she wants help.

     - From the last time she had trouble w/her Zion Memb Portal, she''s been sending everything to them via e-amil.  We did go over making sure she puts the following info into the subject line:  "New Request - Nutritionist", daugher''s name, memb #.  She also knows they will have questions re: when did this start, what has happened, name & contact info for all providers, then they will want pdf or jpeg copies of all detailed invoices, payment receipts, and the order for the Nutritionist.

        One of the items the counselor mentioned to her daughter:  IF she cannot get this under control, she may be looking at an in patient treatment center.  Michelle knows, once they have the ''sharing req'', it will be assigned to someone they work w/at Zion.  That person may be able to help further, however, I do not (nor did Michelle) see anything in the guidelines that address this situation.  [We used anorexia, eating disorders, treatment, etc, as ''Find'' search tools w/nothing coming up.]

     If she has any further issues, she will reach out to us again.     - CA', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-10-09 12:36:44', '2023-10-09 12:36:44'),
