  ('zcrm_1579374000125788038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000115993002', 'Paolo Gramcko-Tursi', NULL, '9-29-2023:  CARI DID NOT HAVE ACCESS TO CRM. HERE ARE HER NOTES:

Originally Angie called sounded quite distraught.  Since I cannot see her CRM or Admin123 files, it felt urgent enough I asked Nahla to take the call after telling her my advice:
     - Find out if Angie is set up w/CirrusMD.  Having access to her records, you should be able to send an invitation, or guide her how to get to them.
     - MAP:  is an option but not set up as an urgent, same day, crisis solution.
Nahla took the call and documented what she went over.     - CA
     Angie called back and Nahla felt she couldn''t help Angie with any other suggestions.  It turns out Angie had already spoken to CirrusMD and was choosing to ignore their advice.  Nahla brought me in.
     I started asking Angie questions:
     - CirrusMD:  I reiterated that these are board certified doctors & if they told her to go to the ER, that really is the doctor''s advice.  She felt the CirrusMD doc did not ask a single question & just flippantly told her to go to the ER.  She had this during her last pregnancy (the baby is just 9month old, so in relatively recent history.) and felt going to the ER that time was pointless because after exposing herself & her unborn baby to 5 hours waiting, their advice did nothing.  She was 8 months along at that point [All of this is by memory.  I could not document while in the call since I don''t have access to her CRM file.]
     - I asked about her obgyn:  This is a new doc.  When she called she felt like they yelled at her, because she''s only 6-wks along and hasn''t even had her initial appt yet.  She was super depressed about not getting help here.
        What about the obgyn that delivered your prev baby = retired, so not an option.
     - Somewhere in the conversation she mentioned tt the Suicide Hotline and that it was not helpful.  So, that was not the solution.
     - Her agitation and the sound of her voice made me feel like she needs to tt someone right now.  So I tried to clarify: Are you trying to find someone right now?  Are you looking for a counselor that can help you once you find a counselor?  etc...  She said they were told our memb has a ''Mental Health Hotline''.  I went over again, that the MAP program w/counseling does not have a hotline.
        Then told her it sounds like you are looking for an immediate option & she agreed.  Since she felt the CirrusMD doc hadn''t even asked any questions I told her I wanted her to reconnect w/CirrusMD.  IF she gets the same doctor, ask for another doctor and/or ask if they have one of their mental health experts available.  Whether they do or do not, to let them know their lack of asking the situation/any questions, has her wanting to talk with another doctor.  
        I reminded her these are board certified doctors, their advice is going to be what she should follow.  She said she would try CirrusMD again to see if they could be of better help.     - CA
A call came in from Zion Healthshare.  Turns out they had Angie on the phone.  Her husband gave her their phone # because they were told there was a ''Mental Health Hotline''.  I explained they may help down the road with sharing, but they are not a Hotline.
     - She still has not reconnected w/CirrusMD.  This time I let her know:  This is extremely time sensitive.  I need you to reconnect with them and ask for a mental health specialist before they leave for the day.  This is as close to a hotline as we can offer.  To please, hang up now and reconnect w/CirrusMD and I told her you need to ask to talk with a ''mental health expert''.
     At this point I just let her know we want for you to have someone to help you.  We are just trying to encourage you to talk to the right people and ask the right things.
     Also, do NOT hesitate to follow their guidance.  If you need to go the ER, I went over how to present.  That we want her to take care of herself. 
     I think she heard me, but I thought she had the time before, so I''m not sure.
     I made sure she knows our hours and that we are here until 8pm her time.  To call us again if she needs to.     - CA', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-09-29 17:44:07', '2023-09-29 17:44:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000125788033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122612001', 'Jennifer Speed', 'CREATED TICKET #3044', '09.29.2023 Jennifer called to have an RX coupon while she was already waiting at the pharmacy. I searched three websites and was able to conjure up 3 coupons from 2 different pharmacies: Publix, Walmart and CVS.
Jennifer also said she took her daughter to a gynocologist, and when they called MPB, they told them that they do not have coverage. It looks like I was the one who spoke to them that day, but according to the notes, I confirmed that our system DOES INDEED share that they have signed up and do currently have Planstin coverage, but it is Planstin''s system that is lacking. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-09-29 17:36:32', '2023-09-29 17:47:22'),
