  ('zcrm_1579374000125775019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000115993002', 'Paolo Gramcko-Tursi', NULL, '09.29.2023 Angie called. Cari picked up. Cari still does not have access to members profiles in CRM NOR ADMIN123. She forwarded the call to me.
Angie is having PPD, her hormones are out of balance. She is seeking therapy sessions, but initially called to ask for the 1-800 hotline number. She had already reached out to CirrusMD, and they guided her to the ER. 
I offered her Mazzitti & Sullivan''s number and to call us back when she has more freedom and time to go over the website''s orientation. 
***************************************************************************************
I realized after the fact that I needed to encourage her to follow the CirrusMD doctor''s advice by going to the ER, so I called her back and shared that with her. I didn''t get a chance to also walked her thru how to present herself, b/c she shared that she had been through this before with her first pregnancy, and when she went to the ER, all they did for her is tell her to breath, and that was after she was waiting for 5 hours. She also shared when she had called the suicide line, they were not helpful either. 
Angie seemed subdued but not balanced emotionally when she shares her experience with the medical profession. The gist of her cathartic share is that what she has reached out to, has not offered her either a solution nor assistance in THAT MOMENT
I was at loss as to how else I could guide and help Angie, and did not want to just leave her with "You need to go to the ER, so you are not alone" message. So, I pulled Cari in to help with a different approach, different verbiage and hopefully soothe Angie and offer her an option. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-09-29 12:11:33', '2023-09-29 16:09:12'),
