  ('zcrm_1579374000125296043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000112459002', 'Cathi Amaya-Sciacca', NULL, '9-20-2023:  Guy called.  Has his derm appt & a few questions:
     - Dermatology:  Going for skin ck.  Discussed "no ins", no "ins" ID card, ''cash-pay'', ask for ''cash-pay'' disc" & IF issue, then we may need to start a ''sharing req''.  Went over 6mos from DOS deadline, so imp to call if they find anything.  Then he''s resp for 1k IUA & a sharing req would help pay for qual items past that.
     - Cardiology ck:  2 yrs ago Labor Day he had a stint put in.  He needs a refill on his medications & wondered how it''s handled.  I let him know it''s similar to the derm appt, BUT, if he did need more & they considered this pre-x, there''s a 1 yr waiting period.  He doesn''t think there''s anything he''ll need to do, so we didn''t go any further.  He''ll save his pymt rec & det inv.
     - Weight loss:  Ozempic.  He tried to see if we could find better pricing here, but when we could not he decided to just pay.  I let him know some items are just tough for us to get better pricing on (especially diabetic items).  But:
     - RXs:  we can ck the expensive items like Ozempic off and on, but his reg RXs we might be able to help on.  He will call to get instructions on how to submit a form (I''m alone today & overwhelmed.  He''s not needing it right now, so was kind enough to talk about this a diff day.)     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-09-20 14:00:14', '2023-09-20 14:33:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000125296038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000080021001', 'Amy Fowler', NULL, '9-20-2023:  RX Quote req for Amy Fowler:
     - Adapalene 0.1% CREAM, 45gms = $50.23 at Kroger on RXGo.
I tt Amy, the gel is less expensive, but may be too drying.  This is a new RX for her, so she''ll keep that in mind, but the doc wrote for the cream.  She went to pick it up at her pharmacy of choice = Pharmacy Care of TN and they wanted ~$240-$.  I found a coupon for this pharmacy, but no contract w/RXGo and still ~$144, so she was good w/using Kroger this time.
        She does have a Costco memb, so she''ll call to see what their memb price is.  The prices I could see there were still ~$156.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-09-20 13:58:40', '2023-09-20 15:32:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000125295013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123941012', 'Jesse Mass', NULL, 'Cancelling', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-09-20 13:47:56', '2023-09-20 13:47:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000125296030', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610497', 'Adam Burstein', NULL, '9-20-2023:  Adam called:
     - He has his colonoscopy sched and when he tt Planstin, they told him he has not been migrated to having no ntwk availabable on his membership.  I let him know I would pass this along to Jennifer who is currently working w/Planstin to find out why they are not seeing our members as having both in & out-of-ntwk available.  IF he has trouble with the out-of-ntwk portion not being paid for (they will bill Planstin directly for him), he will let us know.
        IF they pull a polyp, it become diag anyway.  He know to contact us w/in a few days & we''ll help him sub a ''sharing req''.  That in this scenario, he will be resp for the 1k IUA.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-09-20 13:43:50', '2023-09-20 13:50:31'),
