  ('zcrm_1579374000124764033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000095960001', 'Doug Richter', NULL, '9-11-2023:  tt Shawna w/PT office in AZ looking for approval for Siena''s PT from the auto accident.  We went over how auto accidents are tough because the auto ins carriers are actually resp in the following order:  At-fault, then pers auto if > limit, then their healthcare if there''s more req''d, but that the memb is resp for the first $2500 of that.  Shawna may get a treatment plan to the memb so we can look at sub the ''sharing req'' and getting that started, although, w/all the different parties, it can be a very long & drawn out process.  Shawna seemed to understand where this healthcare stands in the heirarchy, but it''s tough because AZ is a state where no pymts are made by the at fault auto ins until treatment is complete leaving the pymt either being reimb to the patient, or req the provider to wait for 6mos, a yr, or longer.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-09-11 16:10:22', '2023-09-11 16:30:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124763023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000115821001', 'Nichole Baker', NULL, '09.11.2023 Nichole called to learn how to find a provider in network, as she may not have received the email explaining Planstin no longer abides by a network. She needed to go see a doctor for a lump in her breast. I explained there is no more network, and how to maneuver the new system, I explained the difference of the preventative portion and the health-sharing portion of her plan. She needed the card to start the preventative process for a mamm and pap-smear, but did not have one. I called Planstin while she was on hold with me, and Will from Planstin was able to send her both: Virtual and Physical versions. I explained the 6 month deadline for healtsharing bill submission. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-09-11 16:08:13', '2023-09-11 16:08:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124778048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061091330', 'Krista Rogers', NULL, '9-11-23 Hi Wendy,

