  ('zcrm_1579374000124742003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124582013', 'Mark Smith', 'Receipt of Agent Agreement', 'Agent signed agreement came in on 9/9/2023', 'Michele Rebal', 'Michele Rebal', '2023-09-11 07:06:28', '2023-09-11 07:06:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124717080', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077918048', 'Bryan Schiff', NULL, '9/8/2023:  Bryan called & LM for me.  He then talked to Jennifer, but I was on the phone at that time, so I felt I needed to call him back.  I conf lots of what Jennifer told him & walked him thru the options that might work again:
     - Susan & Bryan are due for their colonoscopies:  we talked about how the req for it to be pd is all of the prov (cntr, doc, anesthesiologist) must be willing to bill Planstin directly.  We did disc what happens if they pull a polyp too = chgs to a healthsharing ''sharing req'' w/a 1k IUA for each person that has polyp(s) rem''d.
     - Susan had her mammogram:  Provided her Planstin card & now they are kicking it back as ''cash-pay".  He''s going to call the billing office to see if they didn''t realize it needs to be billed to Planstin.  He will let me know if he needs further asst.', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-09-08 17:55:25', '2023-09-08 21:06:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124717075', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086964002', 'Lani Cordova', NULL, '9/8/2023:  Lani LM that she needs help sub a ''sharing req'' in case the issue continues/comes back.  I called &amp; left her a mess.  It''s late on a Friday, so we can''t do it today anyway.  Asked her to call me next week w/a pen &amp; paper so I can walk her through the process.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-09-08 17:49:44', '2023-09-08 20:59:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124717067', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000103277001', 'Kim Robinson', NULL, '9-8-2023:  Kim called again re: mammogram.  She lives in an area w/a lot of Cleveland Clinic linked centers.  She''s not interested in going there, which I helped her understand will actually help in this situation.  I gave her all the things to say when she''s sched her mamm, so she can make sure she''s covering her basis: 2D ''prev screening'' medical coding, imaging cntr & reading cntr must be willing to bill for her, etc.  If they have trouble understanding, she may have them call us to get info - or - she knows to coach them if the call Planstin re: in & out-of-ntwk being avail.
     - Labs:  Her doc has her going to Quest.  She''s going to get a list of the labs needed, so we can help her find a disc site to get better pricing.  She''ll call us next week while she''s at her computer (she doesn''t have the list of tests yet.  She''ll try for nat lab #s, Quest lab test #s, as well as descriptions so it''s easier for us to confirm we are selecting the proper tests.)
     [- Husb, not a memb, suffered a stroke ~ 2 weeks ago.]     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-09-08 17:35:22', '2023-09-08 17:43:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124717053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098775002', 'Mark Jones', NULL, '9/8/2023:  Mark called me to go over how to handle his ''prev care'' annual appt & a prescription.  We went over no ''prev care'' on Care+.  He knows to present as ''cash-pay'' & ask for a ''cash-pay'' disc.  He will make sure he gets pymt receipts & detailed inv in case something comes up at the appt & it moves to diag or treatment.  
     - He needed to go pick up a prescription the doc just called in for toe fungus.  He likes a pharmacy in ID, but it does not have a contract w/any of the sites (it''s an ind pharmacy): Broulims.  I let him know he can certainly try to use the RXGo coupon I found for this pharmacy, but they do not show having a contract w/the ind pharm, so they may not honor it.  He said he will be in WY this week too, so I sent him a Sav-On coupon as well.  What I could not answer for him, how a state-to-state pharmacy-to-pharmacy transfer would work.  He knows there may be regulations he''ll need to consider if he wants to go that way.  But, he lives right near the state line, so maybe the docs & pharmacies in the area are licensed for both areas?
               - Terbinafine HCL 250mg, #56 tabs = $15.66 at Broulims on RXGo = ID
               - Terbinafine HCL 250mg, #56 tabs = $14.98 at Sav-On on RXGo = WY
                  [For future ref:  Instructions = 2tabs daily x 1 week each month for 4 months.]
    - When Mark started w/MPB, we knew the no ntwk option might become available, so I was able to also disc that has come to fruition.  However, we priced it out (he is self-emp) and it''s enough per year extra, that it may not be worth it unless he''s planning to take adv of the HSA.  He will calculate as he sees the doc''s for his ''prev care'' & let me know.  With a colonoscopy...  maybe it does become worth it.', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-09-08 14:21:22', '2023-09-08 16:24:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124739003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077918048', 'Bryan Schiff', NULL, '9/8/23 - Bryan called in today to say that HCA (Hospital Corporation of America) will not bill Planstin for his preventative care services and he needed to know how to proceed. I advised Bryan that if the hospital is not willing to bill Planstin directly that he may have to find a new provider for his colonoscopy. Bryan wanted to speak with Planstin to see if they could give him any further advice so I transferred him per his request. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-09-08 14:21:14', '2023-09-08 14:21:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124717045', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121237002', 'Nelson Vasconcellos', NULL, '9-8-2023:  Ryan & I finally connected.  He saw the orthopedic spec today (turned out to be in the off of they guy we liked, but this guy spec in his type of injury).  He did tear his achillies, but some of the bone broke off w/the tear.  They are looking at surgery.  I walked him thru how to sub a ''sharing req'': set up Zion Memb Port after requesting an invite thru Zion Cust Srvc, etc.  He thinks he''s just about at his IUA: appt & x-rays $300, air boot doc had him buy $90, MRI soon est at $600 (I''m not sure he even he heard me say this:  "I''m not sure how they look at med equip (ie boot)" but I sugg once they get the ''sharing req'' started, he can call & pay the bal to his 1k IUA so they will just pay from there w/the pre-pd ccs.  Went over how to get estimates (which he''s done already from our conv yesterday) and upload those so he can pay at time of srvcs.  
     - RXs:  I reminded him that if thru all of this they send him to a pharmacy to pickup a prescription, connect w/us so we can see if we can get him the best discounted price available.
     Ryan is super coachable & this is a great plan for someone like him.  Plus, he''s super nice (even when he''s in a lot of pain)!     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-09-08 14:08:28', '2023-09-08 14:14:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124717040', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098495002', 'Rebecca Abma', NULL, '9-8-2023:  Rebecca called.  The hosp has sent her to collections and she''s trying to figure out where he ''med need'' is so she can pay.  I made sure she has Zion''s ph #, their hours, &amp; the ''Med Need'' dept ext, then trans her to them.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-09-08 14:04:05', '2023-09-08 14:04:05'),
