  ('zcrm_1579374000124383011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000056653025', 'Sara Bollmann', NULL, '8-30-2023:  Sara called w/lots of questions:
     - Her advisor, Wendy Scipione, had her call us re: getting a copy of her "ins" card.  She''s on the Care+ program, so there is no "ins" card.  I did some educ on how to present always:  no "ins", no "ins" card, ''cash-pay'', do they offer a ''cash-pay'' disc?, no matter what will always minimally be resp for 1k & even after that 1k mark, she''s still a ''cash-pay'' pt.  IF it moves into an issue (illness, accident, catastrophic), and can/will go over the 1k, we will want to start a ''sharing req'' & need to do that soon after they know there''s something going on.  (ie: finds out she''s preg, call us w/in a few weeks to get everything going).
        After the fact, I let Wendy know she''s a Care+ memb = no "ins" card for ''prev care'' & that I got her all taken care of via a Teams chat.
     - Ob/gyn appt:  going for annual appt & thinks she''s pregnant.  Called thinking she had an "ins" card, but she''s on Care+ so we went over everything.  No ''prev'' in her plan.  If issue comes up and/or she find out she is pregnant, to call us to get whatever ''sharing req'' are needed submitted & don''t wait (issue and/or maternity).  Went over how to ''always'' present (see above).  IF she is pregnant I sugg she ask them for their maternity treatment plan since she''s cash pay & that will help us when we upload the ''sharing req''.
      - Moved to MO w/Dilan Bollman.  She will call tomorrow so we can show her how to update her address.
     - Marrying Dilan Bollman & if she''s preg that may push their wedding date.  We disc that they can comb their plans as significant others before the wedding if they''d like.  Told her I didn''t know which way they would combine since she''s been a memb years and Dilan (although older) has only been a memb for a few mos.  She''s going to tt Dilan & we can disc further about how to proceed if they''d like to combine.
     - HCBB:  Since they are living in a new area, she wanted to conf there is no ntwk for the pregnancy, etc.  We disc HCBB being a good resource.  When she calls back to chg her address, she''ll be at a comp & wants to look at this too.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-30 14:13:41', '2023-08-30 17:16:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124364046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124507177', 'Lisa Triepke', NULL, '8-30-23 Lisa didn''t answer the call for our appt. Leaving her a vm.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-30 13:02:26', '2023-08-30 13:02:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124364041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000056653025', 'Sara Bollmann', NULL, '8-30-23 Left vm to answer her network question now that she''s in Missouri.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-30 12:29:57', '2023-08-30 12:29:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124364036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124369011', 'Rachel Weitz', NULL, '8-30-23 Dan and Rachel chose to go directly to Zion to save over $100 per month for MF. They chose the Essentials $2500 IUA in 40-49 age group which is $350 plus $15 for Teladoc = $365 vs CARE+ which is $480. I couldn''t beat it. So, they enrolled through my link which is connected to me and paid to MPB. They got a Sept. 1st start date. Their only concern was getting access to labs affordably. I told them not to do them in a hospital and to call around for cash pricing. They are all set moving forward.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-30 12:16:51', '2023-08-30 12:16:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124364026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124507067', 'Jeff Barton', NULL, '8-30-23 Jeff enrolled for Oct. 1st start date. He went without ins for 25 years, so he''s used to paying cash and is totally comfortable with that. He''s a little hesitant in how the entire process works to get reimbursed. He understands the value of the MPB Concierge Team for this part. He''s also interested in funding an HSA and possibly an HMA, perhaps even at a higher level than I explained in case of a big medical bill with dental or anything like that. He knows he needs to be an adult and start doing his dental cleanings and such. He joined SECURE $1000/$375.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-30 11:58:18', '2023-08-30 11:58:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124359098', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122995002', 'Erland Slorer', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-08-30 11:46:42', '2023-08-30 11:46:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124383003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000097264002', 'Marilyn Negley', NULL, '8-30-2023:  Debbie from Affiliated Derm called to get "ins" auth for a skin ck, & possible mole biopsy on Joshua.  I told her prev skin cks, etc, generally do not fall into our plan benefits unless the biopsy is cancerous & needs to be rem''d & even then all toll it must be >1k.  That he is a ''cash-pay'' pt, even past the 1k mark.  She will tell Joshua to call us if he has questions or if it does turn out to be something other than general skin maint.  She does not think it will be >1k even w/the one biopsy.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-30 11:36:49', '2023-08-30 11:37:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124382001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086538002', 'Grace Hansen', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat missed', 'Visit ID : 3253 Question : Hi, I''m currently attending school, and they want a copy and coverage of my insurance. Can I have a copy of the coverage, insurance card with an expiration date? It doesn''t show on my card, so I don''t know what to put on the date.', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2023-08-30 11:21:44', '2023-08-30 11:21:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124367011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086538002', 'Grace Hansen', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat missed', 'Visit ID : 3252 Question : Hi, I''m currently attending school and they want a copy and coverage of my insurance. Since I am using MPB Health, what coverage, insurance card, effective, and expiration date of my insurance? It doesn''t show on my card, so I don''t know what to write. Thanks for possible reply.', 'Rod Maxson', 'Rod Maxson', '2023-08-30 11:14:22', '2023-08-30 11:14:22'),
