  ('zcrm_1579374000124292008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000087125001', 'Robert West', NULL, '08.29.2023 Robert called to cancel his membership. I asked him if it had to do with attaining a job with benefits, and that I''m asking to know how to proceed from here. He went on saying kind of, and in addition to that, I filled out a medical need with Zion, since I exceeded my IUA to $1600, and no one responded to my request. I had asked him if he spoke with Leonardo, and he said no, and was adamant on cancelling, as he added in the end that he does have benefits from somewhere else. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-29 17:54:54', '2023-08-29 17:54:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124295054', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165317', 'Melody Fairchild', NULL, '8-29-23 Hi Wendy,
Looking forward to chatting on Sept. 5th about health insurance options.

I wanted to give you the heads up that I am interested in a policy for myself which does not include coverage for doctor visits other than for "catastrophic" events such as accidents or a cancer/disease diagnosis. 

If you are aware of any such policy, I''d be grateful for your looking into the details of it. 

If I am not forced to, I don''t want to spend money for "benefits" of a health plan which I don''t plan to use. I know that Glen wants those and that Dakota should have them, at least for now.

I see "alternative" practitioners (Rolfer, massage therapist, acupuncturist, chiropractor), when I need help with maintaining my health. I don''t see the doctor. Currently, I would not go to the doctor I''ve had, even if I did need to see one. I don''t have a strong relationship with a doctor.

I think the stress of paying so much for something I never use could cause me health problems, if I have any!  :-/

So, if there is a way for me to reduce what I pay for insurance for myself each month, and be able to save that money for when I am too old to work, it would be so much more useful!

Just wanted to share where I am, before our scheduled date. I know I have "vented" to you before when we have a call and I don''t plan to do that. It''s not appropriate and your time and mine is valuable!

It is what it is and I understand that getting a "catastrophic" policy for myself is not too likely... but thought I''d ask, as that is what I truly want...because I know that I will be spending $100-$300.00 /month on rolfing and acupuncture (I never think of going to the doctor if I have pain in my back/knee and can''t do my job or get sick with a cold/the flu, for example...however I did call for antibiotics earlier this year.. but I would be willing to commit to better care of myself in order to avoid the need for a doctor for antibiotics).

I still am totally confused (and so is Glen) by the policy we have.

I have used the phone number to speak to a doctor once the in the past three years. It was a nightmare/long conversation with no help. 

At the very least, if  there is a policy out there which doesn''t have so many different spokes/numbers to call etc, that would be an upgrade. 

Thanks for listening and I appreciate your being there for us!

Melody

Sedera''s prices and Zion''s prices aren''t better even if he joins separately and w/o MPB. That''s not an option. The best choice is to lower their IUA to 2500/$765.  Currently paying $905 at $1000 IUA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-29 17:29:08', '2023-08-29 17:48:08'),
