  ('zcrm_1579374000124205031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000096466002', 'Tamara Doverspike', 'Assigned PW for MPB.Health may no longer be the PW - Memb may have gotten it chg''d', '8-28-2023:  Eric called re: Tamara''s mammogram and cologuard.
     - Tamara had her mammogram - he wanted to know how to get reimb.  He''s going to call the prov & ask them to bill Planstin for them.
     - Tamara''s cologuard he thinks was paid for by Planstin.  We went over the one caveat of having them pay for the cologuard, is then if needed a screening colonoscopy is no longer available because the cologuard used that benefit for this yr.  He seemed to understand.  IF follow-up colonoscopy = diagnostic, then should it > their $2500 IUA, they could have help.
     - MPB.Health Memb Portal:  He was having trouble getting into the portal, thinking that would show him all the components of his membership.*  We did get him into his portal, but I believe his PW chg may have actually worked, because I cannot get into it w/his assigned PW.  He knows that except for pymt history/receipts, & uploading items to us, he can do most everything w/out having to login.
     - Encouraged him to use the concierge proactively, so they know up front the guidelines for ea component since it can be hard to remember w/so much time between doc visits, plus things can chg.
     - *''Welcome Call'' post call e-mail:  Eric''s sure he has this, so he didn''t have me resend.  He''ll ck later.  He knows that this is one of the best places to see everything that is a portion of the memb.
     - *Adv Leslie Jablonski''s site:  I took him here & helped him find the correct place to see what is included in his memb as a back up plan.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-28 13:51:42', '2023-08-28 16:00:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124215003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123199001', 'Carey Reynolds', NULL, '828/23 Carey and Craig are strongly considering SECURE for Oct. 1st onward and perhaps the Cigna plan for September.   Craig sees his cardiologist purely bc there''s family history of heart issues but he hasn''t had any symptoms, diagnosis or treatment. He''s just erring on the side of caution. He does take a statin for elevated cholesterol which is well managed and no hospital visits. Carey sees an NP for mental health meds every 3 months. They both understand that they will need to pay for these visits and not get reimbursed since one is mental health and the other is preventative in nature. They also know that skin checks are not ACA compliant, therefore at their cost at the cash price.  I re-explained the pre-x clause, Life Care and IUA. They will double check their records to make sure they are clear. They will talk and call me likely tomorrow or as soon as they decide.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-28 13:37:30', '2023-08-28 13:37:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124194113', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000125135002', 'Allison Brim', NULL, '8-28-2023 Sent Care+ email overview.', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2023-08-28 13:29:00', '2023-08-28 13:29:00'),
