  ('zcrm_1579374000124094070', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000114129002', 'Stephanie McCarter', NULL, '8-24-2023:  Stephanie sent me an e-mail, completely confused by what is going on w/the billing.  It''s been hard to know, yet, they finished an audit of the books in the last day or two &amp; when I look at her Admin123 acct now, it looks accurate.  I sent her a reply letting her know the amount to anticipate ea monthly contribution &amp; that it''s now the flat amount since she''s moved to ACH.  Asked her to please call us so we can compare what we see if she still has questions.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-25 02:29:06', '2023-08-25 02:29:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124094056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000112459002', 'Cathi Amaya-Sciacca', NULL, '8-24-2023:  Cathi called.
     - Dental ck up: Sounds like they purch''d a sep dental policy.  She''ll call her adv for details.
     - Annual Appt: Planstin = Preventative Only, only time "ins" = Yes; only time "ins" ID card = Yes, Planstin card; do not pay, in ntwk or out-of-ntwk ok as long as doc will bill Planstin, covered ''prev care'' will be pd to the doc dir.  Disc keeping it purely ''prev'' for proper coding.  
     - Cardiac: Husb had a heart attack in Sept 2021 = this will be pre-x.  We disc 1 yr waiting period, then how the phase in works.  She knows until 3/1/2024 = no healthsharing (& it''s not cons prev on Planstin).  Asked if they had their HSA set up (does not sound like they have, but I let her know this is the type of thing those funds can be utilized for).  Told her to see if they set up anything w/Christine for this pre-x, but she does not think so.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-24 16:48:09', '2023-08-24 17:34:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124094051', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000049011710', 'Leah Garcia', NULL, '8-24-2023:  Leah called.  She''s trying to sign up a new memb on the new copay plan &amp; wondered what the $50 charge is.  I let her know the office in FL closed at 5pm Eastern and they would probably be who she needs to speak with (our training isn''t for another week).  However, I made sure she knows how to connect w/Nat Sales Dir (new title?) Wendy Scipione who did yesterday''s training.  Maybe she would be able to answer that question for her.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-24 16:41:11', '2023-08-24 16:41:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124075051', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011521350', 'Shane Michael Sorensen', NULL, '8-24-23 Shane called to figure out what to do about wife Trudy moving forward since he''s moving to Medicare. She is retired and only has SS benefits and no real form of income to show proof of self-employment. She does her annual wellness screenings. So, I explained DIRECT to him and that since she''s retired, I can put her on this membership and it only includes mammo and colonoscopy. I need to mention the additional dr. visit up to $175 as well. Her cost will be $295/$1000 moving forward for Oct. 1st start date. Shane will end Sept. 31st and move to Medicare.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-24 16:07:18', '2023-08-24 16:07:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124094037', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000103252010', 'Jayleen Landstrom', NULL, '8-24-2023:  Jayleen called.  She has more inv, etc. re: Layken''s ER ''med need'' from Feb she needs to submit.  But she''s frustrated:
     - We went over how to call Zion & ask how to add to the new items to her already sub "med need" now that Zion is requiring the ''Zion Memb Portal''.  Allergy tests were done due to the ER visit to see if that''s why he ended-up in the ER.  Then Zion declined it.  She says she tt a man (we are thinking someone at Zion, who agreed she should appeal that decision since it states in their curr guidelines:  "
     - Pd their 1k IUA to Zion after starting initial ''med need''.  But, she''s worried since even w/their guidelines saying it may be shareable in an emerg situation, they are declining it.  We talked in depth about how to readdress this issue.
     - Next step is to look into mold issues.  A chiro that does this is who they are using.  We went over prior appr req''d.  May not look at or reimb for appts prior to that.  Get treatment plan & what to do with it. 
     - HSA:
     - HMA:', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-24 15:49:42', '2023-08-24 18:01:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124094032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058401086', 'Andrew Brinkmeyer', NULL, '8-24-2023:  Andrew gave his MPB.Health ref card to the audiologist (?) provider, who called to see if he had "ins" to pay for his hearing test, hearing aides, etc. 
     - I talked generically about out plan.  Zion shows this in the curr guidelines:
