  ('zcrm_1579374000124094024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000106694002', 'Renee Hornor', NULL, '8-24-2023:  Renee called.  Her husb knee is bothering him (this is a new issue w/this knee) &amp; she wanted to figure out how it works, in ntwk?  out of ntwk?  copay?  etc.  We have not had any training on this, so I got Jennifer Thorin to take the call &amp; trans Renee to her.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-24 13:59:27', '2023-08-24 14:00:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124094016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011862130', 'Marion Steed', NULL, '8-24-2023:  Marion called.  She tt Jennifer Thorin this am & they decided calling CirrusMD would be good.  She did & the doc is prescribing something for shingles for her.  She''s calling Walmart to confirm the # of tabs so I can finish pricing for her.  She''ll ask for me because I have it up & can quickly adj qty when she calls back.     - CA

RX Quote:  Marion called back.  She got the details from Walmart on the RX & w/out a coupon they want $218.  She''s going to look into capsasin cream as well, but I warned her it''s super painful, because the whole point is it is pepper cream that burns the nerve endings.  I suss she ask the pharmacist if that''s still something being used for shingles to kill the nerve endings so it doesn''t hurt so much moment to moment.  We decided to go for the cheapest coupon which was at KS & I taught her how to req a pharmacy-to-pharmacy trans (call KS & ask them to call Walmart for the info).  Here''s the coupon I sent:
     - Famciclovir 500mg, #21 tabs = $16.70 at King Soopers on Sngl Care (even w/out registration) 
     She''s taking 1 tab every 8 hours x 7 days = #21.  The doctor warned her, she''s far enough into the shingles illness, the tabs may not help.  The cheapest Walmart coupon was almost double at $30.86 on RXGo.    - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-24 13:34:54', '2023-08-25 02:40:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124101003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017243295', 'Brooke Spencer', NULL, 'Brooke called to get an update on a Need she submitted a week ago. I warm transferred her to Zion. JAT', 'Jennifer Thorin', 'Jennifer Thorin', '2023-08-24 13:28:49', '2023-08-24 13:28:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124082032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000097703002', 'Laura Most', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation eff 9/1  citing Financial issues I will process', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2023-08-24 13:19:19', '2023-08-24 13:19:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000124094003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122803002', 'Peter Fenwick', NULL, '8-24-2023:  Peter called.  He''s concerned about letting his employer based "trad ins" go before he has his ''Welcome Call'' on Sept 5th.  We disc that the healthsharing is always secondary.  I also mentioned you cannot always backdate cancellation so to ck w/his empl, but he''s fine w/it either way.
     - ''Welcome Call'':  He thinks a diff time would be better, so I recent the invitation & sugg he try to have everyone on the call to hear how to utilize.  I tt Jennifer & she was able to remove his old call sched w/Vanessa, since his new call is already sched w/her.
     - Healthsharing: He wondered what happens when a prov refuses to take cash or won''t work w/you unless you have "ins".  I let him know I''ve seen this a few times, but not often.  In this case, you do have to find another provider.  It''s been rare in my experience though.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-24 13:06:15', '2023-08-24 13:50:27'),
