  ('zcrm_1579374000123915008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123916007', 'Patrick Murphy', NULL, '8-22-23 Patrick enrolled in SECURE $1000/$300 for October 1st onward. He''s super healthy, rarely goes to the dr. When he does he chooses naturopathy, acu, etc. Although he did have kidney stones about 1 year ago. That was resolved and no further issues. He had knee surgery in Jan. 2020. He tends to do his version of wellness through his naturopathic dr. for labs. However he wants to fund his HSA. He is self-employed and doesn''t have an EIN quite yet, so he''ll show other documentation. He does not smoke or use tobacco. He''s 40 and lives in Denver. He also might want dental. he has Anthem right now for $18 a month but it''s out of network. His dentist accepts Delta Dental and the Clear Plan is $39 a month now! So, he''s not sure if it''s worth paying for or not. I also checked 1Dental and his dentist is not in those networks either. Next I can share the HMA. I didn''t do that today. It was too much information all at once. 

Since he could only get an Oct. 1st start date, we had to choose a C4 plan for Sept. He is a Friday Health client but went direct to Friday, not through C4. However, I wanted to offer him Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0 and it was easier to have him create a C4 account. So, he did so, selected the Cigna plan for 1 month. He knows to make sure his payment was accepted and also to cancel sometime in Sept. to end Sept. 30th and move over to MCS. He also won''t have to deal with choosing a new plan in Nov. He''s all set and super happy with my help!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-22 11:20:45', '2023-08-22 11:20:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123915003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123908002', 'Charlotte Westbrook', NULL, '8-22-23 Charlotte enrolled in SECURE HSA $2500/$245 and $100 enrollment fee only.  She was very sweet. She has her own HSA account already from the past and will use that. She was asking about the gov allowing MCS as tax deductible but nothing has changed on that front yet, however I let her know the ins part for $50 is tax ded. But, always talk with a tax professional. She enrolled for an Oct. 1st start date and will cancel Anthem sometime in Sept. for Sept. 30 end date. She will do so and I helped her access the Welcome Call calendar to sign up. She didn''t seem quite ready to pick a time but is confident in how to do so. All set!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-22 11:08:07', '2023-08-22 11:08:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123902013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044842382', 'Amy Tuttle', 'RCVD Perm. Form to Discuss MPB Plan w/ Robert Joyce 8.22.2023', '08.22.2023 BE PATIENT AND DETAILED AND TAKE YOUR TIME w/ this couple.
Amy and Robert called to learn how to submit a medical need with Sedera. It all started with them wanting to access the MPB portal, in order to do that. At first, I dug up Amy''s log in information, offered it to her, and tried to get them to access the portal, not knowing it is a medical need she is trying to commence with Sedera.
I explained how the process of opening a medical need Sedera works, and what Amy will be responsible for when the time of need comes: Call the concierge, we will send an email with instructions, member will complete and reciprocate with Sedera.
Amy needs Robert to speak on her behalf at times, so I sent her the MPB Permission form to discuss the plan.
They have been given an exception by Sedera to submit their long overdue bills of 22K from a hospital ordeal through a medical need. I emailed Amy the instructions to submitting them to Sedera, via CRM.
Both Robert and Amy really want to understand the parts of their plan, but I reassured them that there are way too many moving parts, and that 95% of members call the concierge line first for guidance, as we do not expect the members to remember OR KNOW how to maneuver such a detailed plan at all times.
At the end, both Robert and Amy were in a better place in knowing what their first steps are, when it comes to any actions/services needed towards or from this plan. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2023-08-22 11:02:57', '2023-08-22 15:49:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123895008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000121928001', 'Tanya Hagre', NULL, 'Welcome call complete with Tanya and Neil. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2023-08-22 11:01:25', '2023-08-22 11:18:12'),
