  ('zcrm_1579374000123821035', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086528002', 'Cynthia Colandrea', NULL, '8-21-2023:  
     - Husband:  Oct 12, 2022 = colonoscopy, but he''s receiving the anesthesia bill for ~$2400 now!  We talked & he used the same place they always do & this has never happened before.  The EOB says it''s not covered but doesn''t stipulate why.  She''s going to call Planstin to clarify "why it''s not part of the base benefits".  Maybe they didn''t code it as ''prev care''?  Or the anesthesiologist is out-of-ntwk?
     - Cynthia:  July 3rd, got mamm & ultra sound.  This yr being chg''d $800+ for the ultra sound & last yr it was all of $57. now $270.40 x 2 (=1 for each breast).  Radiology cntr (took 6h to get ahold of them) & this place is not only 5 times thes amount per breast, they chg sep = 2x or 10x total more than last yr.  I let her know there''s not a lot we can do to help here, but hopefully, they will honor the reduced "ntwk" pt resp.   
    - HSA: Haven''t started one yet, but funding this could be a way to at least use tax adv funds.  However, don''t want to have bills go into collections, so be careful.  Disc options here & she knows to touchbase w/acct, fin planner, etc.  To be careful of fees.     - CA', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', 'Cari Adams-Waneka', '2023-08-21 16:30:00', '2023-08-21 16:51:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123867041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123819010', 'Peter Mueller', NULL, '8-21-23 I helped Peter enroll correctly now. I erroneously thought he wanted SECURE and explained how that worked. Then he asked about his lack of self-employment. They do have rental income but no tax docs to show yet. Either way, it makes more sense for him to choose CARE+ since he also won''t fund an HSA. So, we backed up and redid the application for CARE+ before submitting it. Now it was back to the price point he remembered of $265/$1000, plus $125. He''s using a cc for now. I let him know about the fees. I''ve inquired with Steve Schone about cancelling yet again with Zion. He cancelled but the Rep possibly enrolled him again which is not what he intended. I''m awaiting Steve''s response to make sure he''s not double billed with 2 memberships. They also need to back date his start date to Aug. 1st, 2023 since he has Zion only for the month of Aug. I had Peter save the Quick Reference Guide and schedule his Welcome Call for Sept. 1st or thereafter. He''s all set once I make sure his Zion membership is fully cancelled.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-21 15:28:53', '2023-08-21 15:42:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123867031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123908002', 'Charlotte Westbrook', NULL, '8-21-23 Charlotte is 42, lives in NC and is healthy, no pre-x. She wants to be able to fund an HSA and is self-employed. She typically chooses alternative care and naturopathic solutions. She does have a PA she can use for wellness. She rarely goes to the dr. Sounds like she''s leaning towards the $2500/$245 SECURE membership for Oct. 1st start date since she missed the Sept. 1st start date. We have an enrollment appt set for tomorrow.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-21 14:26:53', '2023-08-21 14:26:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000123867026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124293077', 'Paul Dreyer', NULL, '8-21-23 In their C4 account it looks like they''ve had 3 other agents in the past. So, clearly they move around a bunch. They reviewed a bunch of Cigna plans. Then we focused on the Cigna Connect Bronze 7200 vs 0. I encouraged the $0 ded plan since they won''t have to meet a $7200 ded before coins kicks in. The 0 plan is  a little more expensive but worthwhile in my opinion. They will review and let me know what they decide.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2023-08-21 14:18:55', '2023-08-29 16:25:23'),
