  ('zcrm_1579374000123821021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089148022', 'Jeff Weisberg', NULL, '8-21-2023:  Jeff called.  He had his annual doc visit, got the super bill, & wanted to find out how to get reim.  He has Care+ = no prev.  We talked & it does sound like it was 100% prev, so he asked what it takes to get ''prev care'' because he needs to get his colonoscopy.  I sugg it''s best to go over that w/his advisor Michael Montes since they can discuss the diff opt.  Jeff is self-emp, so I briefly told him a tiny bit about HSA Plan & Direct.  He''s not sure so he will call Michael for guidance.  I mentioned at his age of 63, if he can afford to fund the HSA, it''s a great way to have tax adv funds for retirement when Medicare does not pay for everything.
     - We also discussed that getting the ''prev'' for his colonoscopy might do nothing if they pull a polyp(s).  So at least he knows it could move to diagnostic instead of ''prev'' even if he does chg his plan...
     - Chg of pymt form to ACH to get rid of 3% fee:  Told him how to get to the form (his asst is going to process), so I reminded him the form does require his signature.
